{
  "title": "3: Aal-e-Imraan آل عمران",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓ ۚۙ‏(1)\nALEEF-LAAAM-MEEEM\nAlif Laam, Mim\nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۙ الْحَىُّ الْقَيُّوْمُؕ‏(2)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWAL, HAYYUL QAYYOOM\nGod! there is no God but He, the Ever Living the Se1f-Subsistent (The Sustainer of all things)\nنَزَّلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَاَنْزَلَ التَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَۙ‏(3)\nNAZZALA A’LAYKAL KETAABA BIL-HAQQE MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE WA ANZALAT TAWRAATA WAL INJEEL.\nHe hath sent down unto thee the Book with Truth confirming what was before it; And He sent down the Torah and the Evangel\nمِنْ قَبْلُ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ وَاَنْزَلَ الْفُرْقَانَ  ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ ذُو انْتِقَامٍؕ‏(4)\nMIN QABLO HODAL LIN-NAASE WA ANZALAL FURQAAN, INNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEED, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN ZUN-TEQAAM.\nAforetime, a guidance for people and sent down the Distinction (Furqan), Verily for those who disbelieve in the signs of God, for them is a severe punishment; God is Mighty, Lord of Retribution\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَخْفٰى عَلَيْهِ شَىْءٌ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ ؕ‏(5)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYHE SHAY-UN FIL ARZE WA LAA FIS SAMAAA’.\nVerily, God, nothing hidden is there from Him, in the Earth and in the Heavens\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُصَوِّرُكُمْ فِى الْاَرْحَامِ كَيْفَ يَشَآءُ ؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(6)\nHOWAL LAZEE YOSAWWEROKUM FIL ARHAAME KAYFA YASHAAA-O, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nHe it is Who fashioneth you in the wombs (of your mothers) as He liketh; There is no God but HE, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise\nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ مِنْهُ اٰيٰتٌ مُّحْكَمٰتٌ هُنَّ اُمُّ الْكِتٰبِ وَاُخَرُ مُتَشٰبِهٰتٌؕ فَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ زَيْغٌ فَيَتَّبِعُوْنَ مَا تَشَابَهَ مِنْهُ ابْتِغَآءَ الْفِتْنَةِ وَابْتِغَآءَ تَاْوِيْلِهٖۚؔ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ تَاْوِيْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ ؔۘ وَ الرّٰسِخُوْنَ فِى الْعِلْمِ يَقُوْلُوْنَ اٰمَنَّا بِهٖۙ كُلٌّ مِّنْ عِنْدِ رَبِّنَا ۚ وَمَا يَذَّكَّرُ اِلَّاۤ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(7)\nHOWAL LAZEEE ANZALA A’LAYKAL KETAABA MINHO AAYAATUM MOHKAMAATUN HUNNA UMMUL KETAABE WA OKHARO MOTASHAABEHAAT, FA-AMMAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM ZAYGHUN FA-YATTABE-O’ONA MAA TASHAABAHA MINHUB TEGHAAA-AL FITNATE WAB TEGHAAA-A TAAWEELEH, WA MAA YA’LAMO TAAWEELAHUUU ILLAL LAAH, WAR RAASIKHOONA FIL I’LME YAQOOLOONA AAMANNAA BEH, KULLUM MIN I’NDE RABBENAA, WA MAA YAZZAKKARO ILLAAA ULUL ALBAAB.\nHe it is Who hath sent down to thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) ‘the Book of it there are (some) verses decisive these are the Basis of the Book, and others are ambiguous; But those in whose hearts there is perversity, they are after that which is ambiguous therein seeking to mislead and seeking to interpret (to suit their selfish motives) while none knoweth its (hidden) interpretation except God and those firmly rooted in knowledge; say they: “We believe in it, all is from our Lord” but none mindeth save those endowed with (Wisdom)\nرَبَّنَا لَا تُزِغْ قُلُوْبَنَا بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدَيْتَنَا وَهَبْ لَنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً  ۚ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ‏(8)\nRABBANAA LAA TUZEGH QULOOBANAA BA’DA IZ HADAYTANAA WAHAB LANAA MIN LLADUNKA RAHMATAM INNAKA ANTA AL-WAHHAABU.\n(They pray) “Our Lord! Suffer not our hearts to perverse after Thou hast guided (aright) and grant us from unto Thee mercy, for verily Thou, and Thou (Alone) art the Ever- Bestower\nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ جَامِعُ النَّاسِ لِيَوْمٍ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُخْلِفُ الْمِيْعَادَ‏(9)\nRABBANAA INNAKA JAAMEU’U NAASE LE-YAWMIN LAA RAYBA FEEH INNAL LAAHA LAA YUKHLEFUL AL-MEEA’AADA.\nOur Lord! Verily Thou art the Gatherer of mankind unto the Day (of Judgment) about which there is no doubt; (Be Merciful to us then); Verily God faileth not His promise\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْهُمْ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ وَقُوْدُ النَّارِۙ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAN TUGHNEAAA A’NHUM AAMWAALUHUM WA LAA AAWLAADUHUM MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW WA OOLAAA-EKA HUM WAQOODU NAAR.\nVerily, those who disbelieve, never shall their wealth nor their progeny avail them aught against (the Wrath of) God; They and They are the fuel of the (Hell) fire\nكَدَاْبِ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ۚ فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(11)\nKADAABE AALE FIR-A’WNA WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA TOOFAANO LAAHO BEZUNOOBEHEM WAL LAAHO SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nLike unto the wont of the people of Pharaoh and those before them; they belied our signs; so God caught them for their sins; and Verily God is (very) severe in requiting (evil)\nقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا سَتُغْلَبُوْنَ وَتُحْشَرُوْنَ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ‏(12)\nQUL LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO SATUGHLABOONA WA TOHSHAROON ELAA JAHANNAM WA BEASAL MEHAAD.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) to those who disbelieve “ye shall be vanquished and gathered together unto Hell; (what) a wretched resting place (it shall be)\nقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ اٰيَةٌ فِىْ فِئَتَيْنِ الْتَقَتَا ؕ فِئَةٌ تُقَاتِلُ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَاُخْرٰى كَافِرَةٌ يَّرَوْنَهُمْ مِّثْلَيْهِمْ رَاْىَ الْعَيْنِؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصْرِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ  ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّاُولِى الْاَبْصَارِ‏(13)\nQAD KAANA LAKUM TAA-TEENAA FEE FEATAYNE AL-TAQATAA FEATUN TUQAATELU FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAHU KAAFERATUN YYARAWNAHUM MMESLAYHEM RAAAAA AL-A’AYNE WAL LAAHO YUAYDU BENASREH MAN YASHAAA-O INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAE’EBRATAN LEAOOLEAA ULIL ABSAAR.\nIndeed, there was a sign for you in the two hosts (which) met together in the encounter; one host fighting in the path of God and the other disbelieving, (they’) saw them twice their number with their (own) sight of the eye; Verily God aideth with His aid whomsoever He liketh; Indeed in this there is a lesson for those who have (sound) sight\nزُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَوٰتِ مِنَ النِّسَآءِ وَالْبَنِيْنَ وَالْقَنَاطِيْرِ الْمُقَنْطَرَةِ مِنَ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ وَالْخَيْلِ الْمُسَوَّمَةِ وَالْاَنْعَامِ وَالْحَرْثِؕ ذٰ لِكَ مَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۚ وَاللّٰهُ عِنْدَهٗ حُسْنُ الْمَاٰبِ‏(14)\nZUYYENA LIN-NAASE HUBBU ASH-SHAHAWTE MENAL NESAAA-E WAL BANEENA WAL QANAATEERE AL-MUQANTARATE MENAL AZ-ZAHABE WAL FEZZATE WAL KHAYLE AL-MUSAWMATE WAL AANA’AAME WAL HARSE ZAA LEKA MATAAU’U HAYAATID DUNYAA WAL LAAHO I’NDAHU HUSNU AL-MAABE.\n(It has been) made to seem attractively fair unto men, the love of the lusts for women and sons and the hoarded treasures of gold and silver and well-bred horses and cattle and tilth; this is the provision of the life of this world, while God! Verily with Him is the best destination\nقُلْ اَؤُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِخَيْرٍ مِّنْ ذٰ لِكُمْؕ لِلَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا وَاَزْوَاجٌ مُّطَهَّرَةٌ وَّرِضْوَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِالْعِبَادِۚ‏(15)\nQUL AAUNABBEUKUM BE-KHAYRIN MIN ZAA LEKUM LILLAZEENA TAQAW I’NDAL RABBEHIM LAHUM TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WA AZWAAJUM MOTAHHARATUNW WWAREZWAANUN MENAL LAAH WAL LAAHO BASEER BIL-E'BAAD.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Shall I tell you of what is better than these?; for those who take shelter in God are gardens with their Lord, beneath which flow rivers, to abide in them and mates pure, and God’s pleasure; and verily God is well aware of the servants\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِۚ‏(16)\nLAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA INNANAA AAMANNAA FAGH-FIR LANAA ZUNOOBANAA WA QENAA A’ZAABAL NAAR.\nThose who pray saying “O’ Our Lord! Indeed, we believe, so forgive us our sins and save us from the torment of the (Hell) fire\nاَلصّٰبِرِيْنَ وَالصّٰدِقِيْنَ وَالْقٰنِتِيْنَ وَالْمُنْفِقِيْنَ وَالْمُسْتَغْفِرِيْنَ بِالْاَسْحَارِ‏(17)\nAALSSAABEREENA WAS-SAADEQEENA WAL-QAANETEENA WAL MUNFEQEENA WAL MUSTAGHFEREENA BIL-AASHAARE.\nThe patient, and the truthful, and the devout (ones), and those who spend (in the way of God) and those who seek forgiveness e’re dawn\nشَهِدَ اللّٰهُ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۙ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ وَاُولُوا الْعِلْمِ قَآئِمًا ۢ بِالْقِسْطِؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُؕ‏(18)\nSHAHEDAL LAAHO ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA, WAL MALAAEKATO WA OLUL I’LME QAAA-EMAM BIL-QIST, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nGod (Himself) witnesseth that there is no god but HE, and (so do) the angels and those possessed of knowledge, standing firm for justice; (there is) no god but He, the Mighty, the Wise\nاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الْاِسْلَامُ وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ بَغْيًا ۢ بَيْنَهُمْؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(19)\nINNAD DEENA I’NDAL LAAHIL ISLAAM, WA MAKH TALAFAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA ILLAA MIM BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL I’LMO BAGHYAM BAYNAHUM, WA MANY YAKFUR BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE FA-INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nVerily the religion with God is ISLAM (Submission to God’s will), and those whom the Book had been given did not differ but after the knowledge (of the Truth) had come unto them, out of envy among themselves; and whosoever disbelieveth in the signs of God, then, verily, God is quick in reckoning\nفَاِنْ حَآجُّوْكَ فَقُلْ اَسْلَمْتُ وَجْهِىَ لِلّٰهِ وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَنِؕ وَقُل لِّلَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَالْاُمِّيّٖنَ ءَاَسْلَمْتُمْؕ فَاِنْ اَسْلَمُوْا فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوْا ۚ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ الْبَلٰغُ  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِالْعِبَادِ‏(20)\nFA-IN HAAJJOOKA FAQUL ASLAMTO WAJHEAAA LILLAAHE MANIT ATTABAA’ANE WAQUL LIL-LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WA UMMIYYEENA AASLAMTUM FA-IN AASLAMOOA FAQADEH TADAW WA TAWALLAW FA-INNAMAA A’LAYKA BALAAGHUL WAL LAAHO BASEER BIL-E'BAAD.\nBut if they dispute with thee (O’ Our apostle Muhammad!) then say, “I have submitted myself (wholly) to God and (so) doeth everyone who followeth me and say to those who have been given the Book and the unlettered (ones’) “have ye (too) submitted;”? If they submit (themselves to God) then indeed they are rightly guided, and if they turn away, then upon thee is only the delivery (of the message) ‘, and verily, God is well-aware of the servants\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَيَقْتُلُوْنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّۙ وَّيَقْتُلُوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْقِسْطِ مِنَ النَّاسِۙ فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(21)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAKFOROON BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WA YAQTOLOONAN NABIYYEENA BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN WWAYAQTULOONA LAZEENA YAAMUROONA BIL QISTE MENAL NAASE FA-BASH-SHIRHUM BE-A’ZAABIN A’ZAABAN LEEMIN.\nVerily to those who deny the signs of God, and unjustly slay the apostles, and slay those among men who enjoin justice, give tidings to them of a painful chastisement\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(22)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WA MAA LAHUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nThese are they whose works come to naught in this world and in the next; and for them there shall not be any helper\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ يُدْعَوْنَ اِلٰى كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِ لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ يَتَوَلّٰى فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْ وَهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(23)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA OOTOO NASEEBAN MENAL KETAABE YUDA’AWNA ELAA KETAABIL LAAHE LE-YAHKOMA BAYNAHUM SUMMA YATAWALLAA FAREEQUM MINHUM WA HUM MO’REZOON.\nHast thou not (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) seen those (the Jews) who have been given a portion of the Book, when they are summoned unto the Book of God that it may judge between them, then a faction of them turn back while they are those who withdraw\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْا لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ اِلَّاۤ اَيَّامًا مَّعْدُوْدٰتٍ وَغَرَّهُمْ فِىْ دِيْنِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(24)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAALOO LAN LAN TAMASSANAN ILLAA ILLAA MMAA’DOODAATIN WAGHARRAHUM FEE DEENEHEM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nThis, because they say “The (Hell) fire shall by no means touch us but for (some) numbered days, and deceiveth them in the matter of their religion what they have forged\nفَكَيْفَ اِذَا جَمَعْنٰهُمْ لِيَوْمٍ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ وَوُفِّيَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(25)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA JAMAA’NAAHUM LE-YAWMIN LAA RAYBA FEEHE WAWUFFEET KULLO NAFSIM MAA KASABAT WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nHow then (will it be with them) when We shall gather them together for the Day (of Judgment) about which there is no doubt; and every soul shall be paid in full that which it hath earned, and they shall not be wronged?\nقُلِ اللّٰهُمَّ مٰلِكَ الْمُلْكِ تُؤْتِى الْمُلْكَ مَنْ تَشَآءُ وَتَنْزِعُ الْمُلْكَ مِمَّنْ تَشَآءُ وَتُعِزُّ مَنْ تَشَآءُ وَتُذِلُّ مَنْ تَشَآءُ ؕ بِيَدِكَ الْخَيْرُؕ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(26)\nQOLIL LAAHUMMA MAALEKAL MULKE TO’-TIL MULKA MAN TASHAAA-O WA TANZEU’L MULKA MIMMAN TASHAAA-O, WA TO-I’ZZO MAN TASHAAA-O WA TOZILLO MAN TASHAAA-O, BE-YADEKAL KHAYRO, INNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nSay (O’ Apostle Muhammad!) “O’ God! Master of the Kingdom, Thou givest the kingdom unto whomsoever Thou likest and takest away the kingdom from whomsoever Thou likest! Thou exaltest whomsoever Thou likest and abasest whomsoever Thou likest; in Thine hands is all good; verily Thou art over all things Mighty\nتُوْلِجُ الَّيْلَ فِى النَّهَارِ وَتُوْلِجُ النَّهَارَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَتُخْرِجُ الْحَىَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَتُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَىِّ وَتَرْزُقُ مَنْ تَشَآءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(27)\nTOOLEJUL LAYLA FIN NAHAARE WA TOOLEJUN NAHAARA FIL LAYLE WA TUKHREJUL HAYYA MENAL MAYYETE WA TUKHREJUL MAYYETA MENAL HAYYE, WA TARZOQO MAN TASHAAA-O BE-GHAYRE HESAAB.\nThou causest the night to pass into the day, and Thou causest the day to pass into the night, Thou bringest forth the living out of the dead, and Thou bringest forth the dead out of the living, and Thou givest sustenance to whomsoever Thou likest, without measure\nلَا يَتَّخِذِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۚ وَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ فَلَيْسَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ فِىْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَتَّقُوْا مِنْهُمْ تُقٰٮةً  ؕ وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللّٰهُ نَفْسَهٗ ؕوَاِلَى اللّٰهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(28)\nLAA YATTAKHEZE MOAMENOONA KAAFEREEN AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONIL MOAMENEEN WA MAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA FA-LAYSA MENAL LAAHE FEE SHAY-IN ILLAA AN TATTAQOOA MINHUM TUQAATAN WAYUHAZZERUKUMU LAAHO NAFSAH WAALAA LAAHE MASEER.\nSay [O’ Apostle Muhammad!] Whether ye hide what is in your hearts or manifest it, God knoweth it, and He knoweth whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth, and God hath power over all things\nقُلْ اِنْ تُخْفُوْا مَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْ اَوْ تُبْدُوْهُ يَعْلَمْهُ اللّٰهُؕ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(29)\nQUL IN TUKHFOOA MAA FEE SUDOOREKUM AW TUBDOOHU YAA’LAMHU LAAH YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) whether ye conceal what is in your hearts or manifest it, God knoweth it; and knoweth He all that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth; and verily God hath power over all things\nيَوْمَ تَجِدُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ مُّحْضَرًا ۖۚ ۛ وَّمَا عَمِلَتْ مِنْ سُوْٓءٍ ۚۛ  تَوَدُّ لَوْ اَنَّ بَيْنَهَا وَبَيْنَهٗۤ اَمَدًاۢ بَعِيْدًا ؕ وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللّٰهُ نَفْسَهٗؕ وَاللّٰهُ رَءُوْفٌۢ بِالْعِبَادِ ‏(30)\nYAWMA TAJEDU KULLO NAFSIM MAA A’MELAT MIN KHAYRIN MMUHZARAN WA MAA A’MELAT MIN SOOO-IN TAWADDU LAW ANNAL BAYNAHAA BAYNAHU AAMADAN BAE’EEDAN WAYUHAZZERUKUMU LAAHO NAFSAH WAL LAAHO RA-OOFUM BIL-E'BAAD.\n(Remember) the Day (of Judgment) when every soul shall find present whatever it hath wrought of good; and whatever it hath wrought of evil; it will wish that wide were the interval between it, and himself; But God cautioneth you of Himself; and God is affectionate to His (faithful) servants\nقُلْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُحِبُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ فَاتَّبِعُوْنِىْ يُحْبِبْكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوْبَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(31)\nQUL IN KUNTUM TUHEBBOONA LAAHA FAATTABEU’OONEAA YUHBEBKUMU LAAHO WA YAGHFIR LAKUM ZONOOBAKUM WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “If ye do love God, then follow me, God will love you and forgive you your sins; Verily, God is Forgiving, Merciful\nقُلْ اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ ۚ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nQUL AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA YATTABE-U’R FA-IN TAWALLAW FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL KAAFEREEN.\nSay (O’ Qur Apostle Muhammad!) Obey God and the Apostle; but if they turn back, then verily God loveth not the disbelievers\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ اصْطَفٰۤى اٰدَمَ وَنُوْحًا وَّاٰلَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاٰلَ عِمْرٰنَ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(33)\nINNAL LAAHA TAFAA AADAMAL WA ARSALNAA WWAALA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALA E’EMRAANA A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nVerily, God did choose Adam and Noah and the descendants of Abraham and the descendants of Imran above all the worlds\nذُرِّيَّةًۢ بَعْضُهَا مِنْۢ بَعْضٍؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌۚ‏(34)\nZURREETAN BAA’ZUHAA MIN BA’Z WA WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nOffspring, one from the other; and verily God is All-Hearing; All Knowing\nاِذْ قَالَتِ امْرَاَتُ عِمْرٰنَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِىْ بَطْنِىْ مُحَرَّرًا فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّىْ ۚ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(35)\nIZ QAALATE AMRAATU E’EMRAANA RABBE INNEE NAZARTU LAKA MAA FEE BATNEAA MUHARRARAN FA RABBANAA MINNEE INNAKA ANTA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nWhen said (Hanna) the wife of Imran “My Lord! I have vowed unto Thee what is in my womb to be (dedicated) for Thee (exclusively for Thy service) freed (from all worldly responsibilities) therefore accept (it) from me; Verily Thou art the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing\nفَلَمَّا وَضَعَتْهَا قَالَتْ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ وَضَعْتُهَاۤ اُنْثٰىؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْؕ وَ لَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْاُنْثٰىۚ وَاِنِّىْ سَمَّيْتُهَا مَرْيَمَ وَاِنِّىْۤ اُعِيْذُهَا بِكَ وَذُرِّيَّتَهَا مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ الرَّجِيْمِ‏(36)\nFALAMMAA WAZAA’ATHAA QAALAT RABBE INNEE WAZAA’TUHAA AUNSAA WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA WAZAA’AT WA LAYSA AZ-ZAKARU KAALAUNSAA WA INNEE SAMMAYTUHAA MARYAMAL WA INNEE AUE’EEZUHAA BEKA WAZURREETAHAA MENAL SHAYTAANE AR-RAJEEME.\nAnd when she delivered her, she said “My Lord! I have delivered a female (child); and God knew best what she delivered; and the male is not like the female; and I have named it Mary and commend her to Thy protection and also her offspring from Satan the castaway (accursed)\nفَتَقَبَّلَهَا رَبُّهَا بِقَبُوْلٍ حَسَنٍ وَّاَنْۢبَتَهَا نَبَاتًا حَسَنًا ۙ وَّكَفَّلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا ؕ كُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا زَكَرِيَّا الْمِحْرَابَۙ وَجَدَ عِنْدَهَا رِزْقًا ۚ قَالَ يٰمَرْيَمُ اَنّٰى لَكِ هٰذَا ؕ قَالَتْ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(37)\nFATAQABBALAHAA RABBUHAA BEQABOOLIN HASANIN WWAANBATAHAA NABAATAN HASANAN WWAKAFFALAHAA ZAKAREEA KULLAMAA DAKHALA A’LAYHAA ZAKAREEA AL-MEHRAABA WAJADA E’ENDAHAA RIZQAN QAALA YAAMARYAMU ANNAA LAKE HAAZAA QAALAT HOWA MIN I’NDIL LAAH INNAL LAAHA YARZOQO MAN YASHAAA-O BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\nSo accepted her Lord with a gracious acceptance and made her grow up a graceful growing and trusted her into the charge of Zachariah; Whenever Zachariah entered (to see) her in the Sanctuary, (he) found her with a sustenance; He said “O’ Mary! whence (cometh) this to thee?” Said she “It is from God; Verily God provideth whomsoever He liketh without measure\nهُنَالِكَ دَعَا زَكَرِيَّا رَبَّهٗ ۚ قَالَ رَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ ذُرِّيَّةً طَيِّبَةً  ۚ اِنَّكَ سَمِيْعُ الدُّعَآءِ‏(38)\nHONAALEKAB DA-A’A ZAKAREEA WAL QAALA RABBE HAB LEE MIN LLADUNKA ZURREETAN TAYBATAN INNAKA SAMEEU’U AD-DUA’AAE.\nThere did Zachariah pray to his Lord; said he “Lord! grant me from unto Thee a good offspring; Verily, Thou art the Hearer of Prayer\nفَنَادَتْهُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ وَهُوَ قَآئِمٌ يُّصَلِّىْ فِى الْمِحْرَابِۙ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِيَحْيٰى مُصَدِّقًۢا بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَسَيِّدًا وَّحَصُوْرًا وَّنَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(39)\nFANAADATHU TAHMELOHUL WA HOWA QAAEMUN YYUSALLEAA FIL AL-MEHRAABE ANNAL LAAHA YUBASSHERUKA BEEHYAA MOSADDEQAL BEKALEMATIN MENAL LAAHE WASAYDAN WWAHASOORAN WWANABEEA MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nThen called unto him the angels while he stood praying in the sanctuary; “Verily, God giveth thee the glad tidings of (a son) Yahya (John) (who shall be) the confirmer of a Word from God and (besides, he shall be) the honourable and the chaste, and a Prophet from among the virtuous ones\nقَالَ رَبِّ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّقَدْ بَلَغَنِىَ الْكِبَرُ وَامْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرٌؕ قَالَ كَذٰلِكَ اللّٰهُ يَفْعَلُ مَا يَشَآءُ‏(40)\nQAALA RABBE ANNAA LAHUL LEE GHULAAMUN WWAQAD BALAGHANEAAA KEBARO WAAMRAATEAA A’AAQERUN QAALA KAZAALEKA LAAHO YAF-A’LO MAA YASHAAA.\nSaid he “O’ My Lord! How can there be a son (born) to me, when indeed old age hath affected me and my wife is barren?” Said he “Even so God doeth whatsoever He liketh\nقَالَ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِّىْۤ اٰيَةً ؕ قَالَ اٰيَتُكَ اَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلٰثَةَ اَيَّامٍ اِلَّا رَمْزًا ؕ وَاذْكُرْ رَّبَّكَ كَثِيْرًا وَّسَبِّحْ بِالْعَشِىِّ وَالْاِبْكَارِ‏(41)\nQAALA RABBE A’L LEE AAYATAL QAALA AAAYATUKA ALLAA TUKALLEMA NAASA SALAASATA AYYAAMIN ILLAA RAMZAN WAAZKUR RRABBAKA KASEERAA WWASABBEH BIL-A’ASHEAAAE WAL AEBKAARE.\nSaid he “My Lord! appoint Thou a sign for me;” Said He “The Sign for Thee shall be that thou shalt not speak unto men for three days except by signs; and remember God much and glorify Him in the evening and (early) (in) the day break.\nوَاِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يٰمَرْيَمُ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ اصْطَفٰٮكِ وَطَهَّرَكِ وَاصْطَفٰٮكِ عَلٰى نِسَآءِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA IZ QAALATE TAHMELOHUL YAAMARYAMU INNAL LAAHA ASTAFAAKE WATAHHARAKE WAASTAFAAKE A’LAA NESAAE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd (recall O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when said the Angels “O’ Mary! Verily, God hath chosen thee and purified thee and chosen thee above the women of the worlds\nيٰمَرْيَمُ اقْنُتِىْ لِرَبِّكِ وَاسْجُدِىْ وَارْكَعِىْ مَعَ الرّٰكِعِيْنَ‏(43)\nYAAMARYAMU AQNUTEAA LE-RABBEKE WAASJUDEAA WAARKAE’EAA LAAHA RAAKE-E’EN.\nO’ Mary! (for this great grace of thy Lord upon thee) be devout unto thy Lord and prostrate thyself and bow thee down (in prayers) with those who bow down (unto Him)\nذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوْحِيْهِ اِلَيْكَؕ وَمَا كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ اِذْ يُلْقُوْنَ اَقْلَامَهُمْ اَيُّهُمْ يَكْفُلُ مَرْيَمَ وَمَا كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ اِذْ يَخْتَصِمُوْنَ‏(44)\nZAA LEKA MIN AANBAAE GHAYBE NOOHEEHE AELAYKA WA MAA KUNTA LADAYHIM IZ YULQOONA AAQLAAMAHUM AAYHUM YAKFULU MARYAMAL WA MAA KUNTA LADAYHIM IZ YAKHTASEMOON.\nThis is of the news about the (things) unseen which We reveal unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!)’, for thou wast not with them when they did cast their lots with their pens as to which of them should have the charge of Mary; nor wast thou with them when among themselves they disputed\nاِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يٰمَرْيَمُ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنْهُ ۖ اسْمُهُ الْمَسِيْحُ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ وَجِيْهًا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nIZ QAALATE TAHMELOHUL YAAMARYAMU INNAL LAAHA YUBASSHERUKE BEKALEMATIN MINHO ASMUHU AL-MASEEHU E’ESAB ABNU MARYAMAL LAAHE FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WA MENAN MOQARRABEEN.\n(Recall) (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when said the Angels “O’ Mary! Verily, God giveth thee the glad tidings of a Word from Him; whose name shall be Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary; illustrious in this world and in the Hereafter and (shall be) of those near (to God”)\nوَيُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِى الْمَهْدِ وَكَهْلًا وَّمِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(46)\nWAYUKALLEMU NAASA FIL AL-MAHDE WAKAHLAN WWAMENA SAALEHEEN.\nAnd he shall speak to men (alike when) in cradle and when aged; and (he shall be) of the righteous ones\nقَالَتْ رَبِّ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ وَلَدٌ وَّلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِىْ بَشَرٌ ؕ قَالَ كَذٰلِكِ اللّٰهُ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ ؕ اِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(47)\nQAALAT RABBE ANNAA LAHUL LEE WALADUN LAM YAMSASNEAA BASHARUM QAALA KAZAALEKE LAAHO YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nSaid she “O’ My Lord! How can I have a son when, hath not touched me (any) man?” He said “Even so doth God create whatsoever He willeth; When He decreeth a thing then He only saith unto it BE and it IS\nوَيُعَلِّمُهُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَالتَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَۚ‏(48)\nWAYUA’ALLEMUHU KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA TAWRAATA WAL AENJEELA.\nAnd He will teach him the Book and the Wisdom, and the Torah and the Evangel\nوَرَسُوْلًا اِلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرٰٓءِيْلَ ۙ اَنِّىْ قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ۙۚ اَنِّىْۤ  اَخْلُقُ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الطِّيْنِ كَهَیْئَةِ الطَّيْرِ فَاَنْفُخُ فِيْهِ فَيَكُوْنُ طَيْرًاۢ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِۚ وَاُبْرِئُ الْاَكْمَهَ وَالْاَبْرَصَ وَاُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِۚ وَ اُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ وَمَا تَدَّخِرُوْنَۙ فِىْ بُيُوْتِكُمْؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَۚ‏(49)\nWA RASOOLAM ELAA BANEE AESRAAAEELA AANNEAA QAD JETUKUM BE-AAYATIL MIN RABBEKUM AANNEAA AAKHLUQU LAKUM MENAL TEENE KAHAATE TAYRE FAANFUKHU FEEHE FAYAKUN TAYRAN BE-IZNIL LAAHE WAABREU AL-AAKMAHA WAL AABRASA WAAHAAE MAWTAA BE-IZNIL LAAHE WA AUNABBEUKUM BEMAA TAAKULOONA WA MAA TADDAKHEROONA FEE BUYOOTEKUM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LAKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nAnd (appoint him) an Apostle to the children of Israel (and who will declare) “that now I have come unto you with a sign from your Lord; Out of clay will I make for you like the figure of a bird, and I will breathe into it, and it shall becomes flying bird by God’s permission; and I shall heal the blind and the leper and will raise the dead to life by God’s permission; and I will declare to you what ye eat and what ye store up in your houses; Verily, in this will be a sign for you if ye (indeed) be believers.\nوَمُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَىَّ مِنَ التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَلِاُحِلَّ لَكُمْ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ حُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْوَجِئْتُكُمْ بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‏(50)\nWA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAA MENAL WA WALEAUHELLA LAKUM YAWM LAZEE HURREMA A’ALAYKUMWAJETUKUM BE-AAYATIL MIN RABBEKUM FAT-TAQUN LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nAnd (I come) Confirming that which is before me of the Torah: and to allow you some of that which has been forbidden unto you: And I come unto you with a sign from your Lord: take shelter in God, and obey me\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ ؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(51)\nINNAL LAAHA RABBEE WA RABBOKUM FAAA’BUDOOHU HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\nVerily God (HE) is my Lord and (also) your Lord: therefore worship (only) Him; This is the Right Path\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَحَسَّ عِيْسٰى مِنْهُمُ الْكُفْرَ قَالَ مَنْ اَنْصَارِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِؕ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّوْنَ نَحْنُ اَنْصَارُ اللّٰهِۚ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِۚ وَاشْهَدْ بِاَنَّا مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(52)\nFALAMMAA AAHASSA E’EESAA MENHUMU KUFRA QAALA MAN AANSAAREAA ELAL LAAH QAALA AL-HAWAAREEWNA NAHNO AANSAARU LAAHE AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WAASHHAD BE-ANNAA MUSLEMOON.\nAnd when Jesus perceived disbelief on their part: said he, “Who are (there) to be my helpers towards God?” The disciples said “We are the helpers (towards) God! We believe in God! and bear thou witness that we are the ‘Muslims’ unto Him\nرَبَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلْتَ وَاتَّبَعْنَا الرَّسُوْلَ فَاكْتُبْنَا مَعَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(53)\nRABBANAA AAMANNAA BEMAA ANZALTA WAATTABAA’NAA YATTABE-U’R FAAKTUBNAA LAAHA SHAAHEDEEN.\n(And prayed they unto God saying) “O’ Our Lord! we believe in what Thou hast sent down and we follow the Apostle (Jesus); record us then with those who bear witness (unto him)\nوَمَكَرُوْا وَمَكَرَاللّٰهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرُ الْمَاكِرِيْنَ‏(54)\nWA MAKAROO WAMAKARAALLLAAHU WAL LAAHO KHAYRUR AL-MAAKEREENA.\nAnd they (the Jews) planned, and God (also) planned and verily, God is the best of planners\nاِذْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ يٰعِيْسٰۤى اِنِّىْ مُتَوَفِّيْكَ وَرَافِعُكَ اِلَىَّ وَمُطَهِّرُكَ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَجَاعِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْكَ فَوْقَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ ۚ ثُمَّ اِلَىَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَاَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ فِيْمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(55)\nIZ QAALA LAAHO YAAE’EESAA INNEE MUTAWAFFEEKA WARAAFEU’UKA ELAYYA WAMUTAHHERUKA MENAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WAJAAE’ELU LAZEENA ATTABAU’OOKA FAWQA LAZEENA KAFAROO ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE SUMMA ELAYYA MARJE-O’KUM FAAHKUMU BAYNAKUM FEEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nRecall (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when God said: O’ Jesus, I will take thee away and lift thee up unto Me; and purify thee of those that disbelieve, and make those who follow thee triumphant upon those who disbelieve, to the Day of Resurrection. then unto Me shall be your return and I will judge between you in what ye differ\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَاُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(56)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA KAFAROO FAAA’AZZEBUHUM A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WA MAA LAHUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nAnd as to those who disbelieve, I will chastise them with a severe chastisement in this world and the hereafter and for them shall not be any of the helpers\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَيُوَفِّيْهِمْ اُجُوْرَهُمْؕ وَ اللّٰهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(57)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FAYOOFFEEHEM AUJOORAHUM WA LAAHO LAA YOHIBBUL ZAALEMEEN.\nBut to those who believe and do good deeds, He will pay them in full their recompense; and God loveth not the unjust.\nذٰ لِكَ نَتْلُوْهُ عَلَيْكَ مِنَ الْاٰيٰتِ وَ الذِّكْرِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(58)\nZAA LEKA NATLOOHU A’LAYKA MENAL AAYAATE WA AZ-ZEKRE HAKEEM.\nThis, We recite unto thee of the signs and the Wise Reminder\nاِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيْسٰى عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ كَمَثَلِ اٰدَمَؕ خَلَقَهٗ مِنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ قَالَ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(59)\nINNAL MASALA E’EESAA I’NDAL LAAHE KAMASALIL AAADAMA KHALAQAHU MIN TORAABIN SUMMA QAALA LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nVerily, similitude of Jesus with God is as the similitude of Adam; He created him out of dust then said He unto him BE, and he became\nاَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ فَلَا تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْمُمْتَرِيْنَ‏(60)\nAL-HAQQO MIN RABBEKA FALAA TAKUN MENAL MUMTAREEN.\nThe Truth is from thy Lord, therefore be not thou of those of the doubters\nفَمَنْ حَآجَّكَ فِيْهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ فَقُلْ تَعَالَوْا نَدْعُ اَبْنَآءَنَا وَاَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَنِسَآءَنَا وَنِسَآءَكُمْ وَاَنْفُسَنَا وَاَنْفُسَكُمْ ثُمَّ نَبْتَهِلْ فَنَجْعَل لَّعْنَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(61)\nFAMAN HAAJJAKA FEEHE MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-AKA MENAL I’LME FAQUL TA-A’ALAW NADU’U AABNAAANAA WA ABNAAA-AKUM WANESAAANAA WANESAAAKUM WAANFUSANAA WA ANFOSAKUM SUMMA NABTAHEL FANAJA’AL LLAA’NATA LAAHE A’LAL KAAZEBEEN.\nAnd unto him who disputeth with thee therein after the knowledge hath come unto thee, Say! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) (Unto them!) “come ye, let us summon our sons, and (ye summon) your sons, and (we summon) our women and (ye) your women, and (we summon) ourselves and (ye) your selves and then let us invoke and lay the curse of God on the liars!\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْقَصَصُ الْحَقُّ ۚ وَمَا مِنْ اِلٰهٍ اِلَّا اللّٰهُؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(62)\nINNAL HAAZAA LAHOWAL AL-QASASU HAQQO WA MAA MIN ELAAHIN ILLAA LAAH WA INNA LAAHA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nVerily, this is the true narrative; there is no god but God; and verily, God is All-Mighty, All-Wise\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(63)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FA-INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BE-MUFSEDEEN.\nBut if they turn back, then, verily, God knoweth the mischief makers\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ تَعَالَوْا اِلٰى كَلِمَةٍ سَوَآءٍۢ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ اَلَّا نَعْبُدَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهٖ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنَا بَعْضًا اَرْبَابًا مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِؕ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُوْلُوا اشْهَدُوْا بِاَنَّا مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(64)\nQUL YAA AHLA KETAABE TA-A’ALAW ELAA KALEMATIN SAWAAIN BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUM ALLAA NAA’BUDA ILLAA LAAHA WA LAA NUSHREKA BEHI SHAY-ANW WA LAA YATTAKHEZA BAA’ZUNAA BA’ZAN AARBAABAN MIN DOONIL LAAH FA-IN TAWALLAW FA QOOLUN ASHHADOOA BE-ANNAA MUSLEMOON.\nSay; “O’ people of the Book, come ye to a Word Common between us and you, that we worship none but God and shall not associate anything with Him and some of us take not any others for lords other than God;” and if they turn back; then say ye: “Bear ye witness that we are Muslims (those surrendered unto God)\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لِمَ تُحَآجُّوْنَ فِىْۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَتِ التَّوْرٰٮةُ وَالْاِنْجِيْلُ اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(65)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE LEMA TUHAAJJOONA FEE IBRAAHEEMA WA MAA AUNZELATE AT-TAWRAATU WAL AENJEELU ILLAA MIN BAA’DEH AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nO’ ye People of the BOOK! Why dispute ye about Abraham when the Law and the Evangel were not sent down till after him? (what?) Do ye not then understand (so much)?\nهٰۤاَنْتُمْ هٰٓؤُلَآءِ حٰجَجْتُمْ فِيْمَا لَكُمْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ فَلِمَ تُحَآجُّوْنَ فِيْمَا لَيْسَ لَكُمْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(66)\nHAANTUM HAA-OOLAAA-E HAAJAJTUM FEEMAA LAKUM BEHI I’LMUM FALEMA TUHAAJJOONA FEEMAA LAYSA LAKUM BEHI E’ELMUN WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO WA ANTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nLo! ye are those who disputed about which ye had knowledge; but why dispute ye about which ye have no knowledge? And God knoweth and ye know not!\nمَا كَانَ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ يَهُوْدِيًّا وَّلَا نَصْرَانِيًّا وَّ لٰكِنْ كَانَ حَنِيْفًا مُّسْلِمًا ؕ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(67)\nMAA KAANA AEBRAAHEEMU YAHOODEEA WA LAA NASRAANEEA WA LAAKEN KAANA HANEEFAA MMUSLEMAN WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nAbraham was neither Jew nor Christian; but upright in faith (was he) a Muslim; and he was not of the polytheists\nاِنَّ اَوْلَى النَّاسِ بِاِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَلَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُ وَهٰذَا النَّبِىُّ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَلِىُّ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(68)\nINNAL AAWLAA NAASE BE-IBRAAHEEMA LALLAZEENA ATTABAU’OOHU WA NABIYYO WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAAHO WALIYYUL MOAMENEEN.\nVerily, of men the nearest to Abraham, are surely those who followed him and this (Our) Prophet (Muhammad) and those who believe; and verily, God is the Guardian of the faithful\nوَدَّتْ طَّآئِفَةٌ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ لَوْ يُضِلُّوْنَكُمْؕ وَمَا يُضِلُّوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(69)\nWADDAT TAAA-EFATUM MIN AHLIL KETAABE LAW YUZELLOONAKUM WA MAA YUZELLOONA ILLAA ANFOSAHUM WA MAA YASH-O’ROON.\nA group among the people of the Book would fain mislead you; while they mislead not but themselves, but they sense it not\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَاَنْتُمْ تَشْهَدُوْنَ‏(70)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE LEMA TAKFOROONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WA ANTUM TASH-HADOON.\nO’ People of the Book why do ye disbelieve the signs of God while ye yourselves witness (them)?\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لِمَ تَلْبِسُوْنَ الْحَقَّ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُوْنَ الْحَقَّ وَاَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(71)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE LEMA TALBESOONA HAQQA BIL-BAATELE WA TAKTOMOON HAQQA WA ANTUM TA’LAMOON.\nO’ people of the Book: Why confound ye the truth with falsehood, and why hide ye the truth while ye know (it)?\nوَقَالَتْ طَّآئِفَةٌ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ اٰمِنُوْا بِالَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَجْهَ النَّهَارِ وَاكْفُرُوْۤا اٰخِرَهٗ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَۚ ۖ‏(72)\nWA QAALAT TAAA-EFATUM MIN AHLIL KETAABE AAMENOO BIL-LAZEE UNZELA A’LAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAJHAL AN-NAHAARE WAAKFUROOA AAAKHERAH LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd said a group of the people of the Book, “Believe in what hath been sent down to the believers at daybreak and deny it at its close perchance (by this device) they may return (to disbelief)\nوَلَا تُؤْمِنُوْۤا اِلَّا لِمَنْ تَبِعَ دِيْنَكُمْؕ قُلْ اِنَّ الْهُدٰى هُدَى اللّٰهِۙ اَنْ يُّؤْتٰٓى اَحَدٌ مِّثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ اَوْ يُحَآجُّوْكُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْؕ قُلْ اِنَّ الْفَضْلَ بِيَدِ اللّٰهِۚ يُؤْتِيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ ۚۙ‏(73)\nWA LAA LAM TOAMENOO ILLAA LEMAN-Y TA-BE-A’ DEENAKUM QUL INNAL HODAA HODAL LAAHE AN YYUTAAA AHAD MISLA MAA MAA OOTEETUM AW YUHAAJJOOKUM I’NDAL RABBEKUM QUL INNAL FAZLA BEEDE LAAHE YUTEEHE MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\n(And they say) And believe not in any but those who follow your religion; Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Verily, the (true) guidance is the guidance from God; ‘(envy ye) that to any other (also) hath been given the like of what hath been given to you; or (fear ye that) they (would) dispute you in the presence of your Lord”. Say, Thou, - “Grace is in the hands of God; He granteth it unto whomsoever He liketh; and verily, God is Omniscient, All-Knowing\nيَّخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(74)\nYYAKHTASSU BE-RAHMATEHI MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO ZUL FAZLIL A’ZEEM.\nHe singleth out for His mercy whomsoever He liketh; and verily, God is (the Lord) of Great Grace\nوَمِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ مَنْ اِنْ تَاْمَنْهُ بِقِنْطَارٍ يُّؤَدِّهٖۤ اِلَيْكَۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اِنْ تَاْمَنْهُ بِدِيْنَارٍ لَّا يُؤَدِّهٖۤ اِلَيْكَ اِلَّا مَا دُمْتَ عَلَيْهِ قَآئِمًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْا لَيْسَ عَلَيْنَا فِىْ الْاُمِّيّٖنَ سَبِيْلٌۚ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ وَ هُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(75)\nWA MIN AHLIL KETAABE MAN IN TAAMANHU BEQENTAARIN YYUADDEH ELAYKA WA MINHUM MAN IN TAAMANHU BEDEENAARIN LAA YUADDEH ELAYKA ILLAA MAA DUMTA A’LAYHE QAAA-EMAA ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAALOO LAYSA A’LAYNAA FEE UMMIYYEENA SABEELUN WA YAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nAnd from among the people of the Book are such whom if thou entrust (even) a heap of Gold, he will restore it unto thee: and from among them are such whom if thou entrust (even) a dinar, he will not restore it unto thee unless thou keepeth standing firmly upon him demanding it; This because they say “It is not incumbent on us” (to be faithful) to the ignorant and they utter a lie against God while they know (what they do is wrong)\nبَلٰى مَنْ اَوْفٰى بِعَهْدِهٖ وَاتَّقٰى فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(76)\nBALAA MAN AWFAA BEA’AHDEH WAT TAQAA FA-INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nYea, whoso keepeth his promise and guardeth himself (against evil), for verily, God loveth those who guard themselves (against evil)\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَشْتَرُوْنَ بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ وَاَيْمَانِهِمْ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا اُولٰٓئِكَ لَا خَلَاقَ لَهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ وَلَا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَلَا يَنْظُرُ اِلَيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَلَا يُزَكِّيْهِمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(77)\nINNAL LAZEENA YASHTAROONA BEA’AHDE LAAHE WAAYMAANEHEM SAMANAN QALEELAA OOLAAA-EKA LAA KHALAAQA LAHUM FIL AAKHERATE WA LAA YOKALLEMOHOMUL LAAHO WA LAA YANZORUL ELAYHIM YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA LAA YOZAKKEEHIM WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nVerily, they who barter their covenant with God and their oaths for a paltry price; These! are they for whom there is no share in the hereafter, and God will not speak to them will not look towards them on the Day of Resurrection; nor will He purify them, and for them (shall be) a grievous punishment\nوَاِنَّ مِنْهُمْ لَفَرِيْقًا يَّلْوٗنَ اَلْسِنَتَهُمْ بِالْكِتٰبِ لِتَحْسَبُوْهُ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِۚ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِۚ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ وَ هُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA INNA MINHUM LAFAREEQAN YYALWNA AALSENATAHUM BE-KETAABE LETAHSABOOHU MENAL KETAABE WA MAA HOWA MENAL KETAABE WA YAQOOLOONA HOWA MIN I’NDIL LAAHE WA MAA HOWA MIN I’NDIL LAAHE WA YAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nAnd verily among them is a group who twist their tongues (with) the book that ye may reckon it to be of the Book, but it is not of the Book, and they say, “It is from God”, and it is not From God; and they tell a lie against God while they know (it well)\nمَا كَانَ لِبَشَرٍ اَنْ يُّؤْتِيَهُ اللّٰهُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ ثُمَّ يَقُوْلَ لِلنَّاسِ كُوْنُوْا عِبَادًا لِّىْ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنْ كُوْنُوْا رَبَّانِيّٖنَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تُعَلِّمُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَ وَبِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَدْرُسُوْنَۙ‏(79)\nMAA KAANA LEBASHARIN AN YYUTEEHU LAAHO KETAABA WAL HUKMA WA NOBUWWATA SUMMA YAQOOLAR LIN-NAASE KOONOO E’EBAADAN LEE MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAAKIL KOONOO RABBAANEENA BEMAA KUNTUM TUA’ALLEMOONA KETAABA WA BEMAA KUNTUM TADRUSOONA.\nIt is not for a man, that God should give him the Book and Judgment and apostleship and yet he should say to people, “Be ye worshippers of me, besides God’s”; but rather, (he would say) “Be ye godly what ye teach the Book and what ye read (yourselves)\nوَلَا يَاْمُرَكُمْ اَنْ تَتَّخِذُوا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ وَالنَّبِيّٖنَ اَرْبَابًا ؕ اَيَاْمُرُكُمْ بِالْكُفْرِ بَعْدَ اِذْ اَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA LAA YAAMURAKUM AN TATTAKHEZOOA AL-MALAAAEKATA WAN NABIYYEEN AARBAABAN AAYAAMURUKUM BIL-KUFRE BA’DA IZ ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nAnd nor would he enjoin you that ye should take the Angels and the Apostles for lords: What! would he enjoin you with disbelief after ye are ‘Muslims’ unto God?\nوَاِذْ اَخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِيْثَاقَ النَّبِيّٖنَ لَمَاۤ اٰتَيْتُكُمْ مِّنْ كِتٰبٍ وَّحِكْمَةٍ ثُمَّ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مُّصَدِّقٌ لِّمَا مَعَكُمْ لَتُؤْمِنُنَّ بِهٖ وَلَتَنْصُرُنَّهٗ ؕ قَالَ ءَاَقْرَرْتُمْ وَاَخَذْتُمْ عَلٰى ذٰ لِكُمْ اِصْرِىْؕ قَالُوْۤا اَقْرَرْنَا ؕ قَالَ فَاشْهَدُوْا وَاَنَا مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(81)\nWA IZ AAKHAZA LAAHO MEESAAQA NABIYYEENA LAMAA AAATAYTUKUM MIN KETAABIM WWAHEKMATIN SUMMA JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUM MMUSADDEQUN LEMAA MA-A’KUM LATUMENUNNA BEHI WALATANSURUNNAH QAALA AAQRARTUM WAAKHAZTUM A’LAA ZAA ZAALEKUM AESREAA QAALOO AAQRARNAA QAALA FAASHHADOOA ANAT MA-A’KUM MENAL SHAAHEDEEN.\nAnd when God took the pledge of the Prophets, “Verily, what I have given you of the Book and (of) Wisdom - then cometh a Prophet unto you confirming that which is with you; Ye shall surely believe in him and help him”; He said: “Do you affirm and accept to take up (on these terms’) my burden (which I lay upon you)”; They said “We affirm;” He said: “Bear ye then the witness (among yourselves) and I am a witness with you\nفَمَنْ تَوَلّٰى بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(82)\nFAMAN TAWALLAA BA’DA ZAA LEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nTherefore, whoever turneth away after this, these are they that are the transgressors\nاَفَغَيْرَ دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ يَبْغُوْنَ وَلَهٗۤ اَسْلَمَ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ طَوْعًا وَّكَرْهًا وَّاِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(83)\nAAFAGHAYRA DEEN LAAHE YABGHOONA WA LAHU ASLAMA MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE TEYAA WWAKARHAN WA ELAYHE YARJEO’ON.\nSeek they other than the religion of God? when unto Him submitteth whosoever is in the heavens and the earth, willingly or unwillingly and unto Him they shall be returned\nقُلْ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَالْاَسْبَاطِ وَمَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مُوْسٰى وَ عِيْسٰى وَالنَّبِيُّوْنَ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْ لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(84)\nQUL AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WA MAA UNZELA A’LAYNAA WA MAA UNZELA A’LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA AESMAAE’EELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WA ASBAATE WA MAA OOTEYA MOOSAA WA E’EESAA WA NABIYYOONA MIN RABBEHIM LAA NOFARREQO BAYNA AHADIM MINHUM WA NAHNO LAHU MUSLEMOON.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) (unto the people) “We believe in God, and in what hath been sent down to us, and what hath been sent down to Abraham and Ishmael, and Isaac, and Jacob, and the Tribes, and in what was given to Moses, and Jesus and the Prophets from their Lord, we make no difference between any of them, and we unto Him are Muslims\nوَمَنْ يَّبْتَغِ غَيْرَ الْاِسْلَامِ دِيْنًا فَلَنْ يُّقْبَلَ مِنْهُ ۚ وَهُوَ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(85)\nWA MAN YYABTAGHE GHAYRA AL-AESLAAME DEENAN FALAN YYUQBALA MINHO WA HOWA FIL AAKHERATE MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nAnd whosoever Seeketh any religion other than Islam (total resignation unto God) never shall it be accepted from him, and in the next world he shall be among the losers\nكَيْفَ يَهْدِى اللّٰهُ قَوْمًا كَفَرُوْا بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِهِمْ وَشَهِدُوْۤا اَنَّ الرَّسُوْلَ حَقٌّ وَّجَآءَهُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(86)\nKAYFA YAHDIL LAAHO QAWMAN KAFAROO BA’DA EEMAANEHIM WASHAHEDOOA ANNAL YATTABE-U’R HAQQUWN WWAJAAAHUMU AL-BAYNAATU WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nHow shall God guide a people who disbelieved after their (once) believing and after they had borne witness that the Apostle (Muhammad) was true, and clear evidence had come unto them; and God guideth not people (who are) unjust\nاُولٰٓئِكَ جَزَآؤُهُمْ اَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةَ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(87)\nOOLAAA-EKA JAZAAUHUM ANNAL A’LAYHIM LAA’NATA LAAHE WAL MALAA-EKATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’ENA.\nThese, their return is that upon them shall rest the curse of God and the angels and of mankind together\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ۚ لَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَۙ‏(88)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA LAA YOKHAFFAFO A’NHOMUL A’ZAABO WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nTherein shall they abide, their torment shall not be lightened, nor shall they be respited\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ وَاَصْلَحُوْا  فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(89)\nILLAA LAZEENA TAABOO MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA WA ASLAHOO FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nExcept those who after this repent and amend; for verily God is Forgiving Merciful!\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِهِمْ ثُمَّ ازْدَادُوْا كُفْرًا لَّنْ تُقْبَلَ تَوْبَتُهُمْۚ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الضَّآ لُّوْنَ‏(90)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BA’DA EEMAANEHIM SUMMA AZDAADOOA KUFRAN LAN-Y TUQBALA TAWBATUHUM WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL LAMENAZ LLOONA.\nVerily, those who disbelieve after their believing, then increase in their infidelity; never shall their repentance be accepted, and these are they who have gone astray\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ فَلَنْ يُّقْبَلَ مِنْ اَحَدِهِمْ مِّلْءُ الْاَرْضِ ذَهَبًا وَّلَوِ افْتَدٰى بِهٖ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌۙ وَّمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(91)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA MAATOO WA HUM KUFFAARUN FALAN YYUQBALA MIN AAHADEHEM MMELU ARZE ZAHABAN WWALAWE AFTADAA BEHI OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM WA MAA LAHUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nVerily, those who disbelieve and die while they are disbelievers, never shall be accepted even earthful of gold from any of them, if he should offer it in ransom, these, for them awaiteth a painful torment and for them (there shall be) no helpers\nلَنْ تَنَالُوا الْبِرَّ حَتّٰى تُنْفِقُوْا مِمَّا تُحِبُّوْنَ ؕ  وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ شَىْءٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِهٖ عَلِيْمٌ‏(92)\nLAN TANAALOOA BIRRA HATTAA TUNFEQOO MIMMAA TUHEBBOONA WA MAA TUNFEQOO MIN SHAY-IN FA-INNAL LAAHA BEHI A’LEEM.\nNever shall ye attain to righteousness until ye give (in charity) out of what ye love…\nكُلُّ الطَّعَامِ كَانَ حِلًّا لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اِلَّا مَا حَرَّمَ اِسْرَآءِيْلُ عَلٰى نَفْسِهٖ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تُنَزَّلَ التَّوْرٰٮةُ ؕ قُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِالتَّوْرٰٮةِ فَاتْلُوْهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(93)\nKULLO AT-TAA’AAME KAANA HELLAN LLEBANEAA ISRAAA-EELAZ ILLAA MAA HARRAMA AESRAAAEELU A’LAA WA MIN QABLE AN TUNAZZALA AT-TAWRAATU QUL FAATOO BE-WA FAATLOOHAA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAll food was allowed to the children of Israel except what Israel (Jacob) had (himself) forbidden before the Torah (Pentateuch); was sent down; Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad to the Jews) “Bring ye hither then the Torah and read it (out), if ye be truthful.\nفَمَنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَؔ‏(94)\nFAMANE’ TARAA A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AZ-ZAALEMOONA.\nThen whoever fabricateth a lie about God, after this, these it is that are the unjust.\nقُلْ صَدَقَ اللّٰهُ فَاتَّبِعُوْا مِلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا ؕ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(95)\nQUL SADAQAL LAAHO FA TABE-O’O MILLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “God hath spoken the Truth, follow therefore the creed (Islam) of Abraham the upright in faith; and he was not of the polytheists ”.\nاِنَّ اَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ وُّضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِىْ بِبَكَّةَ مُبٰرَكًا وَّهُدًى لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَۚ‏(96)\nINNAL AWWALA BAYTIYN WWUZEA’A LIN-NAASE LALLAZEAA BEBAKKATA MUBAARAKAN WWAHUDAN LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nVerily, the First House made for mankind is the one at Mecca, Blessed and a Guidance for the worlds.\nفِيْهِ اٰيٰتٌ ۢ بَيِّنٰتٌ مَّقَامُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَۚ  وَمَنْ دَخَلَهٗ كَانَ اٰمِنًا ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ عَلَى النَّاسِ حِجُّ الْبَيْتِ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ اِلَيْهِ سَبِيْلًا ؕ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِىٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(97)\nFEEHE AAYAATUM BAYYENAATUN MMAQAAMU IBRAAHEEMA WA MAN DAKHALAH KAANA AAMENANW LILLAAHE A’LAL NAASE HEJJU BAYTE MANIS ASTATAAA’A ELAYHE SABEELAA WA MAN KAFARA FA-INNAL LAAHA GHANIYYUN A’NIL A’ALAMEEN.\nIn it are clear signs; the standing place of Abraham; and whoever entereth it is secure; and (purely) for God, is incumbent upon mankind, the pilgrimage to the House, for those who can afford to journey thither; And whoever denieth then Verily, God is ‘Self-sufficiently independent of the worlds.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ ۖ وَاللّٰهُ شَهِيْدٌ عَلٰى مَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(98)\nQUL YAA AHLA KETAABE LEMA TAKFOROONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WAL LAAHO WA A’LAA MAA TA’MALOON.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “O’ People of the Book! why disbelieve ye the Signs of God? While Verily, God is a witness upon what ye do.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لِمَ تَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ تَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا وَّاَنْتُمْ شُهَدَآءُ ؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(99)\nQUL YAA AHLA KETAABE LEMA TASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE MAN AAMANA TABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN WA ANTUL SHUHADAAU WA MAA LAAHO BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “O’ people of the Book! why hinder ye, him who believeth, from the path of God? and seek to make it crooked? whereas ye are its witness; And God is not heedless of what ye do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ تُطِيْعُوْا فَرِيْقًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ يَرُدُّوْكُمْ بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِكُمْ كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(100)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN TO-TEE-O’O FAREEQAM MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA YARUDOOKUM BA’DA EEMAANEKUM KAAFEREEN.\nO’ ye who believe! if ye obey a group among those who have been given the Book, they will turn you back into infidels after your believing.\nوَكَيْفَ تَكْفُرُوْنَ وَاَنْتُمْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتُ اللّٰهِ وَفِيْكُمْ رَسُوْلُهٗ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّعْتَصِمْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدْ هُدِىَ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(101)\nWA KAYFA TAKFOROONA WA ANTUM TUTLAA A’LAYKUM AAYAATUL LAAHE WA FEEKUM RASOOLUH WA MAN YYAA’TASEM BIL-LAAHE FAQAD HUDEAAA ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nHow can ye disbelieve, while the signs of God are recited unto you, and His Apostle (Muhammad) is among you? Whoever holdeth fast unto God, is already guided to the Right path.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ تُقٰتِهٖ وَلَا تَمُوْتُنَّ اِلَّا وَاَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(102)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO TAQUL LAAHA HAQQA TUQAATEH WA LAA TAMOOTUNNA ILLAA WA ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nO’ ye who believe, fear God as He deserves to be feared\nوَاعْتَصِمُوْا بِحَبْلِ اللّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا وَّلَا تَفَرَّقُوْا وَاذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ كُنْتُمْ اَعْدَآءً فَاَ لَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوْبِكُمْ فَاَصْبَحْتُمْ بِنِعْمَتِهٖۤ اِخْوَانًا ۚ وَكُنْتُمْ عَلٰى شَفَا حُفْرَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ فَاَنْقَذَكُمْ مِّنْهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(103)\nWAAA’TASEMOOA BEHABLE LAAHE JAMEE-A’A WA LAA TAFARRAQOOA WA KOROO NEA’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ KUNTUM AAA’DAAAN FA-ALQEEHE LLAFA BAYNA QOLOOBEKUM FA-ASBAHTUM BENEA’MATEH AEKHWAANAN WA KUNTUM A’LAA SHAFAA HUFRATIN MENAL NAAR FAANQAZAKUM MINHAA KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AAYAATEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\nAnd hold ye fast by the cord of God All together, and be not divided (among yourselves) and remember the bounty of God bestowed upon you, when ye were enemies (of each other) He united your hearts together with (mutual) love, and thus, by His favour ye have become brethren and (while) ye were on the brink of the pit of the Hell-Fire then He delivered you therefrom; Thus, doth God clearly explaineth His signs for you, so that ye may be guided.\nوَلْتَكُنْ مِّنْكُمْ اُمَّةٌ يَّدْعُوْنَ اِلَى الْخَيْرِ وَيَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(104)\nWALTAKUN MINKUM UMMATUN YAD-O’ONA ELAL KHAYR WAYAAMUROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WAYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nAnd that there should be among you a group who call (mankind) unto virtue and enjoin what is good and forbid wrong; and these are they who shall be successful.\nوَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّذِيْنَ تَفَرَّقُوْا وَاخْتَلَفُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌۙ‏(105)\nWA LAA TAKOONOO TAKOONOO TAFARRAQOOA WA TALAFOO MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL AL-BAYNAATU WA OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd be not like those who got divided and disagreed after clear evidences have come unto them; and these! for them is a great torment.\nيَّوْمَ تَبْيَضُّ وُجُوْهٌ وَّتَسْوَدُّ وُجُوْهٌ  ؕ فَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اسْوَدَّتْ وُجُوْهُهُمْ اَكَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِكُمْ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(106)\nYAWMA TABYAZZU WOJOOHUN-Y WWATASWADDU WOJOOHUN-Y FA-AMMAA LAZEENA ASWADDAT WOJOOHOHUM AAKAFARTUM BA’DA EEMAANEKUM FAZOOQOOA A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROONA.\n(On) the Day when some faces will be bright and some faces will be black! And as to those whose faces will have turned black; (it will be said unto them) “What! Did you disbelieve after believing? Taste ye, then, the chastisement for what ye were disbelieving.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ ابْيَضَّتْ وُجُوْهُهُمْ فَفِىْ رَحْمَةِ اللّٰهِ ؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(107)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA ABYAZZAT WOJOOHOHUM FA FEE RAHMATE LAAHE HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nAnd as to those whose faces shall have become white they shall be in the Mercy of God; therein shall they abide.\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ اللّٰهِ نَتْلُوْهَا عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ ظُلْمًا لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(108)\nTILKA AAYAATUL LAAHE NATLOOHAA A’LAYKA BIL-HAQ WA MAA LAAHO YOREEDO ZULMAWN LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nThese are the signs of God, We recite them unto thee in truth; And God intendeth not injustice to mankind.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(109)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nGod’s is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; and unto God (only) shall all matters return.\nكُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ اُمَّةٍ اُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ تَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَتَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَتُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِؕ وَلَوْ اٰمَنَ اَهْلُ الْكِتٰبِ لَڪَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْؕ مِنْهُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَاَكْثَرُهُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(110)\nKUNTUM KHAYRAZ UMMATIN AUKHREJAT LIN-NAASE TAAMUROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WATANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WATUMENOONA BILLAAH WA LAW AAMANA AAHLU KETAABE LAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM MENHUMU MOAMENOONA WAAKSARUHUMU FAASEQOON.\nYe are the best group that hath been brought forth for mankind: Ye enjoin goodness and ye forbid evil, and ye believe in God; And if the people of the Book had (also) believed (similarly) it had surely been better for them; of them (only some) are believers and most of them are perverse.\nلَنْ يَّضُرُّوْكُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَذًىؕ وَاِنْ يُّقَاتِلُوْكُمْ يُوَلُّوْكُمُ الْاَدْبَارَ ثُمَّ لَا يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(111)\nLAN YYAZURROOKUM ILLAA AZAA WA YYUQAATELOOKUM YOOLLOOKUMU ADBAAR SUMMA LAA HUM YUNSAROON.\nNever shall they harm you except slight injury; and if they fight with you, they shall turn their backs to you; then they shall not be helped.\nضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ اَيْنَ مَا ثُقِفُوْۤا اِلَّا بِحَبْلٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَحَبْلٍ مِّنَ النَّاسِ وَبَآءُوْ بِغَضَبٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَسْكَنَةُ  ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَيَقْتُلُوْنَ الْاَنْۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِمَا عَصَوْا وَّكَانُوْا يَعْتَدُوْنَ‏(112)\nZUREBAT A’LAYHEMUL ZILLATO AYNA MAA SOQEFOO ILLAA BEHABLIN MENAL LAAHE WAHABLIN MENAL NAASE WA BAAA-OO BE-GHAZABIM MENAL LAAHE WA ZOREBAT A’LAYHEMUL AL-MASKANATU ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAANOO YAKFOROON BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WA YAQTOLOONAN AL-AANBEEAAAA BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN ZAA LEKA BEMAA A’ASAWA WWAKAANOOA YA’TADOON.\nAbasement is made to cleave to them wherever they are found, except under a covenant with God and a covenant with men, and they have drawn down the wrath of God (on them): (Besides) humiliation is stamped upon them; This because they used to disbelieve in the signs of God, and slew the prophets unjustly; This because they disobeyed and used to transgress.\nلَيْسُوْا سَوَآءً ؕ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ اُمَّةٌ قَآئِمَةٌ يَّتْلُوْنَ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ اٰنَآءَ الَّيْلِ وَ هُمْ يَسْجُدُوْنَ‏(113)\nLAYSOOA SAWAAAN MIN AHLIL KETAABE UMMATUN QAAEMATUN YYATLOONA AAYAATIL LAAHE AAANAAA LAYLE WA HUM YASJODOONA.\nThey are not alike; of the people of the Book, is a group (so) upright (in faith) that they recite the signs of God all along the night, and prostrate themselves in adoration.\nيُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُسَارِعُوْنَ فِىْ الْخَيْرٰتِ ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(114)\nYOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA YAAMUROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WAYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WAYUSAAREU’OONA FEE AL-KHAYRAATE WA OOLAAA-EKA MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nThey believe in God and in the Last Day (of Resurrection), and enjoin goodness and forbid evil, and hasten to do good deeds; and these are of the righteous ones.\nوَمَا يَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلَنْ يُّكْفَرُوْهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(115)\nWA MAA YAFA’ALOOA MIN KHAYRIN FALAN YYUKFAROOHU WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BE-MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd whatever good they do; they shall not be denied (the meed); God knoweth The pious ones.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْهُمْ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا  ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(116)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAN TUGHNEAAA A’NHUM AAMWAALUHUM WA LAA AAWLAADUHUM MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW WA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nBut as for those who disbelieve, never shall their possessions nor their children, avail them anything, against God; They shall be the inmates of the Hell-fire, therein they shall abide.\nمَثَلُ مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا كَمَثَلِ رِيْحٍ فِيْهَا صِرٌّ اَصَابَتْ حَرْثَ قَوْمٍ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَاَهْلَكَتْهُ ؕ وَمَا ظَلَمَهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَلٰكِنْ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(117)\nMASALUL MAA YUNFEQOONA FEE HAAZEHE HAYAATID DUNYAA KAMASALIL REEHIN FEEHAA SERRUN AASAABAT HARSA QAWMIN ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM FAAHLAKATHU WA MAA ZALAMAHUMU LAAHO WA LAAKIL ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nThe likeness of what they spend in this life of the world is like that of a freezing wind, which smiteth upon the tilth of a people who have wronged themselves and destroyed it; God did no injustice to them, it was they who are doing injustice to themselves.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوْا بِطَانَةً مِّنْ دُوْنِكُمْ لَا يَاْلُوْنَكُمْ خَبَالًا ؕ وَدُّوْا مَا عَنِتُّمْۚ قَدْ بَدَتِ الْبَغْضَآءُ مِنْ اَفْوَاهِهِمْ  ۖۚ وَمَا تُخْفِىْ صُدُوْرُهُمْ اَكْبَرُؕ قَدْ بَيَّنَّا لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(118)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA BETAANATAN MIN DOONEKUM LAA YAALOONAKUM KHABAALAN WADDOOA MAA A’ANETTUM QAD BADATE AL-BAGHZAAU MIN AFWAA-HEHIM WA MAA TUKHFEAA SODOOROHUM AKBAR QAD BAYYANNAL LAKOMUL AAYAATE IN KUNTUM TA’QELOON.\nO’ ye who have believed! take not intimates, other than your fellow-believers, They will not fail to corrupt you; they wish what distresseth you (the most); Their spite hath already shewn itself out of their mouths, but that which is concealed in their breasts is greater still; indeed We have made clear the signs unto you, if ye would understand.\nهٰۤاَنْتُمْ اُولَاۤءِ تُحِبُّوْنَهُمْ وَلَا يُحِبُّوْنَكُمْ وَتُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْكِتٰبِ كُلِّهٖ ۚ وَاِذَا لَقُوْكُمْ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا  ۖۚ وَاِذَا خَلَوْا عَضُّوْا عَلَيْكُمُ الْاَنَامِلَ مِنَ الْغَيْظِؕ قُلْ مُوْتُوْا بِغَيْظِكُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ ۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(119)\nHAANTUM AOOLAAE TUHEBBOONAHUM WA LAA YUHEBBOONAKUM WATUMENOONA BE-KETAABE KULLEH WA EZAA LAQOOKUM QAALOO AAMANNAA WA EZAA KHALAW A’AZZOOA A’LAYKOMUL AL-AANAAMELA MENAL GHAYZ QUL MOOTOO BEGHAYZEKUM INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nLo! Ye are those who love them, but they love you not though ye believe in the entire Book, and when they meet you, they say: “We believe”; but when they are apart, they bite their finger’s ends at you in rage against you; Say (O’ Apostle Muhammad!)” “Die ye in your rage;” Verily God well-knoweth whatever is in (people’s) breasts.\nاِنْ تَمْسَسْكُمْ حَسَنَةٌ تَسُؤْهُمْ وَاِنْ تُصِبْكُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَّفْرَحُوْا بِهَا ۚ وَاِنْ تَصْبِرُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا لَا يَضُرُّكُمْ كَيْدُهُمْ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطٌ‏(120)\nIN TAMSASKUM HASANATUL TASUHUM WA TUSEBKUM SAYYE-ATUM YYAFRAHOOA BEHAA WA TASBEROOA WA TATTAQOO LAA YAZURRUKUM KAYDUHUM SHAY-ANW INNAL LAAHA BEMAA YA’MALOON MOHEETUM.\nIf any good (even) toucheth, you it grieveth them, and if ill afflicteth you, they rejoice at it; But if ye be patient and guard yourselves (against evil) their craft shall not harm you; for verily whatever they do, God is comprehensive of (it).\nوَاِذْ غَدَوْتَ مِنْ اَهْلِكَ تُبَوِّئُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ مَقَاعِدَ لِلْقِتَالِؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(121)\nWA IZ GHADAWTA MIN AAHLEKA TUBAWU MOAMENEEN MAQAAE’EDA LIL-QETAALE WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd when thou didst set forth from thy family at early dawn that thou prepare for the believers the encampment for the battle; and God is The Hearer, The Knower.\nاِذْ هَمَّتْ طَّآئِفَتٰنِ مِنْكُمْ اَنْ تَفْشَلَا ۙ وَاللّٰهُ وَلِيُّهُمَا ؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(122)\nIZ HAMMAT TTAAEFATAANE MINKUM AN TAFSHALAA WAL LAAHO WALEEHUMAA WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\n(Remember O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) When two groups of you had thought to flinch, and God was the Guardian of both; in God should the believers trust.\nوَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَّاَنْتُمْ اَذِلَّةٌ  ۚ فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(123)\nWA LAQAD NASARAKUMU LAAHO BEBADRIN WA ANTUL AAZELLATUN FA TAQUL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nIndeed God hath succoured you at ‘Badr’ when ye were contemptibly weak; so take shelter in God, so that ye may be thankful.\nاِذْ تَقُوْلُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَلَنْ يَّكْفِيَكُمْ اَنْ يُّمِدَّكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِثَلٰثَةِ اٰلَافٍ مِّنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ مُنْزَلِيْنَؕ‏(124)\nIZ TAQOOLO LIL-MOAMENEEN AALAN YYAKFEEKUM AN YYUMEDDAKUM RABBOKUM BE-SALAASATE AAALAAFIN MENAL MALAA-EKATE MUNZALEENA.\n(Remember O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when thou didst say to the believers, “Doth it not suffice you that your Lord should help you with three thousand angels sent down (from heaven)?\nبَلٰٓى ۙ اِنْ تَصْبِرُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا وَيَاْتُوْكُمْ مِّنْ فَوْرِهِمْ هٰذَا يُمْدِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِخَمْسَةِ اٰلَافٍ مِّنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ مُسَوِّمِيْنَ‏(125)\nBALAAA IN TASBEROOA WA TATTAQOO WAYAATOOKUM MIN FAWREHEM HAAZAA YUMDEDKUM RABBOKUM BEKHAMSATE AAALAAFIN MENAL MALAA-EKATE MUSAWMEENA.\nAye! if ye be steadfast and take shelter in God and if the enemy come upon you in this very dashing manner, your Lord will help you with five thousand (such) angels distinguished who will be (fully equipped).\nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بُشْرٰى لَكُمْ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوْبُكُمْ بِهٖؕ وَمَا النَّصْرُ اِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِۙ‏(126)\nWA MAA JAA’ALAHU LAAHO ILLAA BUSHRAA LAKUM WALETATMAENNA QOLOOBOKUM BEH WA MAA AN-NASRU ILLAA MIN I’NDIL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nGod did not effect this but as good tidings for you, and that thereby your hearts might rest assured; and (there) is no succour but from God, the Mighty, the Wise.\nلِيَقْطَعَ طَرَفًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَوْ يَكْبِتَهُمْ فَيَنْقَلِبُوْا خَآئِبِيْنَ‏(127)\nLEEQTAA’A TARAFAN MENAL LAZEENA KAFAROO AW YAKBETAHUM FAYANQALEBOOA KHAAEBEENA.\nThat He might cut off a part of those who believe not or cast them down so that they may retire disappointed.\nلَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ شَىْءٌ اَوْ يَتُوْبَ عَلَيْهِمْ اَوْ يُعَذِّبَهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(128)\nLAYSA LAKA MENAL AL-AAMRE SHAY-UN AW AW A’LAYHIM AW YUA’AZZEBAHUM FA INNAHUM ZAALEMOON.\nNothing of the authority is for thee at all, whether He turneth unto them (mercifully) or chastiseth them, for verily, they are transgressors.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَ يُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(129)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ YAGHFERO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YO-A’ZZEBO MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd God’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever in the earth; He forgiveth whomsoever He pleaseth and punisheth whomsoever He pleaseth, for, Verily, God is the Oft-Forgiving, the Merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَاْكُلُوا الرِّبٰٓوا اَضْعَافًا مُّضٰعَفَةً  وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَۚ‏(130)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAAKULOOA REBAA AZ-A’AFAN MMUZAAA’AFATAN WAT TAQUL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO’ ye who believe! Devour not interest doubling it over and again, and take shelter in God that ye may be successful.\nوَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِىْۤ اُعِدَّتْ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَۚ‏(131)\nWAT TAQUL NAARAL LATEE O-I’DDAT LIL KAAFEREENA.\nFear ye the Hell-fire that is prepared for the disbelievers.\nوَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَۚ‏(132)\nWAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA YATTABE-U’R LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nAnd obey God and the Apostle (Muhammad) that ye may be shown Mercy.\nوَسَارِعُوْۤا اِلٰى مَغْفِرَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُۙ اُعِدَّتْ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(133)\nWASAAREU’OOA ELAA MAGHFERATIN MIN RABBEKUM WA JANNATIM A’ARZUHAA AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL O-I’DDAT LILMUTTAQEEN.\nAnd hasten unto (the means to obtain) forgiveness from your Lord and Paradise vast as the heavens and the earth, prepared for the pious ones.\nالَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ فِى السَّرَّآءِ وَالضَّرَّآءِ وَالْكٰظِمِيْنَ الْغَيْظَ وَالْعَافِيْنَ عَنِ النَّاسِؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَۚ‏(134)\nLAZEENA YUNFEQOONA FIL AS-SARRAAE WAZ ZARRAAA-E WAL KAAZEMEENA AL-GHAYZA WAL A’AAFEENA A’NIL NAAS WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nThose who spend (in alms) alike in prosperity and straitness, and who restrain (their) anger, and forgive (the faults of) men; for God loveth those who do good (to others).\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا فَعَلُوْا فَاحِشَةً اَوْ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ ذَكَرُوا اللّٰهَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوْا لِذُنُوْبِهِمْ وَمَنْ يَّغْفِرُ الذُّنُوْبَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ  وَلَمْ يُصِرُّوْا عَلٰى مَا فَعَلُوْا وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(135)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA FAA’ALOOA FAAHESHATAN AW ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM ZAKAROOA LAAHA FAASTAGHFAROOA LEZUNOOBEHEM WA MAN YYAGHFERU AZ-ZUNOOBA ILLAA LAAHO WA LAM YUSERROOA A’LAA MAA FAA’ALOOA WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nAnd those who, when they do a shameful deed or commit a wrong to their (own) selves, remember God and implore for pardon for their sins; and who forgiveth sins except God? And who persist not (intentionally), in what they have done (amiss) while they know it.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ جَزَآؤُهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ وَنِعْمَ اَجْرُ الْعٰمِلِيْنَؕ‏(136)\nOOLAAA-EKA JAZAAUHUM MAGHFERATUNW MIN RABBEHIM WA LAHUM TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WA NE’MA AJRUL AL-A’AAMELEENA.\nAs for these, their reward is pardon from their Lord and gardens ‘neath which rivers flow to abide therein; And excellent is the reward of those who act (righteously).\nقَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ سُنَنٌ ۙ فَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(137)\nQAD KHALAT MIN QABLEKUM SUNANUN FA SEEROO FIL ARZE FANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MOKAZZEBEENAZ.\nIndeed, there have already been before you examples, travel ye therefore in the earth and see what hath been the end of the rejecters of (the Apostles of God)\nهٰذَا بَيَانٌ لِّلنَّاسِ وَهُدًى وَّمَوْعِظَةٌ لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(138)\nHAAZAA BAYAANUN LIN-NAASE WA HODANW WWAMAWE’EZATUN LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nThis is (only) a clear statement (of events) for mankind, and a guidance and admonition for the pious ones.\nوَلَا تَهِنُوْا وَ لَا تَحْزَنُوْا وَاَنْتُمُ الْاَعْلَوْنَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(139)\nWA LAA TAHENOOA WA LAA TAHZANOO WAANTUMU AL-AAA’LAWNA IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nAnd lose ye not heart and grieve ye not, for ye shall gain the upper hand, if ye (only) be (true) believers\nاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِّثْلُهٗ ؕ وَتِلْكَ الْاَيَّامُ نُدَاوِلُهَا بَيْنَ النَّاسِۚ وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَدَآءَؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(140)\nIN YYAMSASKUM QARHUN FAQAD MASSAN QAWMAZ QARHUN MMESLUH WA TILKAL AL-AAYAMU NUDAAWELUHAA BAYNA NAASE WALEEA’LAMA LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO WAYATTAKHEZA MINKUM SHUHADAAA WAL LAAHO LAA YOHIBBUL ZAALEMEEN.\nIf a wound hath afflicted you, a wound similar hath also afflicted the people (disbelievers); And these days (of varying fortunes) We bring about among men by turns, And that God may know those who have (sincerely) believed, and that He may take witnesses from among you; and God loveth not the unjust.\nوَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَيَمْحَقَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(141)\nWALEEMAHHESA LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO WAYAMHAQA KAAFEREEN.\nAnd that God may purge those who believe and destroy the infidels.\nاَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ اَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ جَاهَدُوْا مِنْكُمْ وَيَعْلَمَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(142)\nAM HASIBTUM AN TADKHOLUL JANNATA WA LAMMAA YAA’LAME LAAHO LAZEENA JAAHADOO MINKUM WAYAA’LAMA MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nImagine ye (O’ Muslims!) that ye (all) would enter Paradise? When God knoweth yet not those (of you) who strove hard among you (in His way) and knoweth (also) the steadfast?\nوَلَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تَلْقَوْهُ فَقَدْ رَاَيْتُمُوْهُ وَاَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(143)\nWA LAQAD KUNTUM TAMANNAWNA MAWTA MIN QABLE AN TALQAWHU FAQAD RAAYTUMOOHU WA ANTUM TANZOROON.\nAnd ye did indeed desire for death ere ye met it, so indeed ye have now seen it, even while ye look (at it).\nوَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ اِلَّا رَسُوْلٌ  ۚ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُؕ اَفَا۟ئِنْ مَّاتَ اَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِكُمْؕ وَمَنْ يَّنْقَلِبْ عَلٰى عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَّضُرَّ اللّٰهَ شَيْئًا ؕ وَسَيَجْزِى اللّٰهُ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(144)\nWA MAA MOHAMMADUN ILLAA RASOOLUM QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHE AR-RUSULU AAFAAEN MMAATA AW QOTELAL ANQALABTUM A’LAA AAA’QAABEKUM WA MAN YYANQALEB A’LAA A’LAA FALAN YYAZURRA LAAHA SHAY-ANW WASAYAJZEAA LAAHO ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nAnd Muhammad is not but an Apostle, (Other) apostles have already passed away prior to him; Therefore, if he dieth or be slain, will ye turn upon your heels? And he who turneth upon his heels will by no means do harm to God in the least, and shortly will God reward the grateful ones.\nوَمَا كَانَ لِنَفْسٍ اَنْ تَمُوْتَ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ كِتٰبًا مُّؤَجَّلًا ؕ وَ مَنْ يُّرِدْ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا نُؤْتِهٖ مِنْهَا ۚ وَمَنْ يُّرِدْ ثَوَابَ الْاٰخِرَةِ نُؤْتِهٖ مِنْهَا ؕ وَسَنَجْزِى الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(145)\nWA MAA KAANA LE-NAFSIM AN TAMOOTA ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAHE KETAABAA MMUAJJALAN WA MAN YYURED SAWAABA DUNYAA NUTEH MINHAA WA MAN YYURED SAWAABA AAKHERATE NUTEH MINHAA WASANAJZEAA ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nIt is not for any soul to die except by God’s permission, (according to) the Book that fixes the term (of life); He who desireth (his) reward in this world, We give him thereof and he who desireth (his) reward in the hereafter, We give him thereof! And shortly We shall reward the grateful ones.\nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ نَّبِىٍّ قٰتَلَ ۙ مَعَهٗ رِبِّيُّوْنَ كَثِيْرٌ ۚ فَمَا وَهَنُوْا لِمَاۤ اَصَابَهُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا ضَعُفُوْا وَمَا اسْتَكَانُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(146)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN NNABEAAAIN QAATALA MA-A’HU REBBEEWNA KASEERUM FAMAA WAHANOOA LEMAKH AASAABAHUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA MAA ZAU’UFOOA WA MAA ASTAKAANOOA WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nHow many a prophet hath fought with whom were myriads of Godly men, and they lost not heart at what befell them in the way of God nor did they weaken, nor did they demean themselves (before their enemies); And God loveth the steadfast ones.\nوَمَا كَانَ قَوْلَهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْا رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا وَاِسْرَافَنَا فِىْۤ اَمْرِنَا وَ ثَبِّتْ اَقْدَامَنَا وَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(147)\nWA MAA KAANA QAWLAHUM ILLAA AN QAALOO RABBANAA FIR LANAA ZUNOOBANAA WAASRAAFANAA FEE AAMRENAA WA SABBET AQDAAMANAA WAN SURNAA A’LAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd their saying was nothing but that they prayed “O’ Our Lord! forgive us our sins and our excesses in our affairs and set our feet firm and help us against the disbelieving people.\nفَاٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا وَحُسْنَ ثَوَابِ الْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(148)\nFAATAAHUMU LAAHO SAWAABA DUNYAA WAHUSNA SAWAABE AAKHERATE WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd God gave them the reward in this world and an excellent reward of the hereafter; And verily God loveth those who do good (to others).\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ تُطِيْعُوا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يَرُدُّوْكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِكُمْ فَتَنْقَلِبُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(149)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN TUTEEU’OOA LAZEENA KAFAROO YARUDOOKUM A’LAA AAA’QAABEKUM FATANQALEBOOA KHAASEREEN.\nO’ ye who believe! if ye obey the disbelievers they will make you to turn on your heels so ye will turn back losers.\nبَلِ اللّٰهُ مَوْلٰٮكُمْۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ النّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(150)\nBALIL LAAHO MAWLAAKUM WA HOWA KHAYRUR AN-NAASEREENA.\nNay! God is your Guardian and He is the Best of the Helpers.\nسَنُلْقِىْ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا الرُّعْبَ بِمَاۤ اَشْرَكُوْا بِاللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ سُلْطٰنًا ۚ وَمَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُؕ وَ بِئْسَ مَثْوَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(151)\nSANULQEE FEE QOLOOBIL LAZEENA KAFARUL ROA’BA BEMAA ASHRAKOO BIL-LAAHE MAA LAM YUNAZZEL BEHI SULTAANAN WAMAAWAAHUMU AN-NAARU WA MASALUL MASWAA ZAALEMEEN.\nWe will cast a dread into the hearts of the disbelievers because they have associated with God, that for which He hath sent down no authority and their abode shall be the fire; And how bad is the abode of the unjust.\nوَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَعْدَهٗۤ اِذْ تَحُسُّوْنَهُمْ بِاِذْنِهٖۚ حَتّٰۤی اِذَا فَشِلْتُمْ وَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِى الْاَمْرِ وَعَصَيْتُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَاۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ مَّا تُحِبُّوْنَؕ مِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّرِيْدُ الدُّنْيَا وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّرِيْدُ الْاٰخِرَةَ  ۚ ثُمَّ صَرَفَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ لِيَبْتَلِيَكُمْۚ وَلَقَدْ عَفَا عَنْكُمْؕ وَ اللّٰهُ ذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(152)\nWA LAQAD SADAQAKUMU LAAHO WA’DAHU IZ TAHUSSOONAHUM BE-IZNEH HATTAA EZAA FASHELTUM WATANAAZAA’TUM FIL AL-AAMRE WAA’ASAYTUM MIN BA’DE MAA AARAAKUM MAA TUHEBBOONA MINKUM MAN YYUREEDU DUNYAA WA MINKUM MAN YYUREEDU AAKHERATA SUMMA SARAFAKUM A’NHUM LEEBTALEEKUM WA LAQAD A’AFAA A’ANKUM WA LAAHO ZOO FAZLIN A’LAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd indeed hath God made good to you His promise, when ye were extirpating them by His permission, till when ye flinched and disputed about the command, and ye disobeyed, after that (He) had showed you that which ye loved; Of you some desire this world, and some hereafter, Then Ye turned you away from them (ran away), so that He may test (prove) you (in the sincerity of your faith): and (in spite of this) He hath forgiven you; And verily God is the Lord of Grace for the believers.\nاِذْ تُصْعِدُوْنَ وَلَا تَلْوٗنَ عَلٰٓى اَحَدٍ وَّالرَّسُوْلُ يَدْعُوْكُمْ فِىْۤ اُخْرٰٮكُمْ فَاَثَابَكُمْ غَمًّا ۢ بِغَمٍّ لِّكَيْلَا تَحْزَنُوْا عَلٰى مَا فَاتَكُمْ وَلَا مَاۤ اَصَابَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(153)\nIZ TUSE’EDOONA WA LAA TALWNA A’LAA AHADIM WWAALRRASOOLU YADU’OOKUM FEE AUKHRAAKUM FAASAABAKUM GHAMMAN BEGHAMMIN LLEKAYLAA TAHZANOO A’LAA MAA FAATAKUM WA LAA MAA AASAABAKUM WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nRemember when ye ran off precipitately on the heights and (even) looked not back any one, while the Apostle (Muhammad) calling you from the rear! So He hath inflicted (upon) you with anguish after anguish, that ye might (learn) not to grieve at what ye lose, nor at what befell you; and God is (fully) aware of what ye do.\nثُمَّ اَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ الْغَمِّ اَمَنَةً نُّعَاسًا يَّغْشٰى طَآئِفَةً مِّنْكُمْۙ وَطَآئِفَةٌ قَدْ اَهَمَّتْهُمْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ يَظُنُّوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ ظَنَّ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِؕ يَقُوْلُوْنَ هَلْ لَّنَا مِنَ الْاَمْرِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ قُلْ اِنَّ الْاَمْرَ كُلَّهٗ لِلّٰهِؕ يُخْفُوْنَ فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ مَّا لَا يُبْدُوْنَ لَكَؕ يَقُوْلُوْنَ لَوْ كَانَ لَنَا مِنَ الْاَمْرِ شَىْءٌ مَّا قُتِلْنَا هٰهُنَا ؕ قُلْ لَّوْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ بُيُوْتِكُمْ لَبَرَزَ الَّذِيْنَ كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَتْلُ اِلٰى مَضَاجِعِهِمْۚ وَلِيَبْتَلِىَ اللّٰهُ مَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْ وَلِيُمَحِّصَ مَا فِىْ قُلُوْبِكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(154)\nSUMMA ANZALAL A’LAYKUM MIN BA’DE AL-GHAMME AAMANATAN NNUA’AASAN YYAGHSHAA YASTAZ-E’FO MINKUM WA TAAA-EFATUM QAD AAHAMMATHUM ANFOSOHUM YAZUNNOONA BIL-LAAHE GHAYRA HAQQE ZANNAS AL-JAAHELEETE YAQOOLOONA HAL LANAA MENAL AL-AAMRE MIN SHAYIN QUL INNAL AMRA KULLAH LIL-LAAH YUKHFOONA FEE ANFOSEHIM MAA LAA YUBDOONA LAK YAQOOLOONA LAW KAANA LANAA MENAL AL-AAMRE SHAY-UN MAA QUTELNAA HAAHUNAA QUL LAW KUNTUM FEE BUYOOTEKUM LABARAZA LAZEENA KOTEBA A’LAYHEMUL AL-QATLU ELAA MAZAAJEE’EHEM WALEEBTALEAAA LAAHO MAA FEE SUDOOREKUM WALEEMAHHESA MAA FEE QULOOBEKUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nThen after the anguish God sent down security upon you: (in the form of) slumber over-come upon a group of you, while the other group who cared only for their own selves-thinking quite unjustly about God; thoughts of ignorance; Say they “Is there anything for us in the authority?” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Verily the authority resteth wholly with God;” They hid in their selves what they would not reveal unto thee, Say they “Had we had anything in the authority, we would not have been slain at this place;” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!)”Had ye remained in your homes they who were decreed to be slain would have gone forth to the places where they (now) lie; and that God might test what was in your breasts and he might purge what was in your hearts; for verily God knoweth what is (hidden) in your breasts.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَوَلَّوْا مِنْكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعٰنِۙ اِنَّمَا اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ بِبَعْضِ مَا كَسَبُوْا ۚ وَلَقَدْ عَفَا اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(155)\nINNAL LAZEENA TAWALLAW MINKUM YAWMA AL-TAQAA AL-JAMA’AANE INNAMAA ASTAZALLAHUMU SHAYTAANO BE-BA’ZIL MAA KASABOO WA LAQAD A’AFAA LAAHO A’ANHUM INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR HALEEM.\nVerily those of you who turned back on the day (of Uhud) when the hosts met, (it was) only Satan made them slip on account of some of their (sinful) actions; But indeed God hath pardoned them; For God is Oft-Forgiving, Forbearing.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَكُوْنُوْا كَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَقَالُوْا لِاِخْوَانِهِمْ اِذَا ضَرَبُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ اَوْ كَانُوْا غُزًّى لَّوْ كَانُوْا عِنْدَنَا مَا مَاتُوْا وَمَا قُتِلُوْا ۚ لِيَجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ ذٰ لِكَ حَسْرَةً فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ وَ اللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(156)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAKOONOO TAKOONOO KAFAROO WA QAALOO LE-IKHWAANEHIM EZAA ZARABOOA FIL ARZE AW KAANOO GHUZZAN LAW KAANOO E’ENDANAA MAA MAATOOA WA MAA QUTELOOA LEEJA’ALA LAAHO ZAA LEKA HASRATAN FEE FEE WAL LAAHO YOHYEE WA YOMEET WA LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\nO’ Ye who believe! be ye not like the disbelievers who said of their brethren when they travel in the earth or engaged in fight (in the way of God) “Had they been with us they would not have died and had not been slain” so that God may make this an intense regret in their hearts; and it is God Who giveth life and causeth to die; and God beholdeth what all ye do.\nوَلَئِنْ قُتِلْتُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَوْ مُتُّمْ لَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَحْمَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّا يَجْمَعُوْنَ‏(157)\nWA LAIN QUTELTUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE AW MUTTUM LAMAGHFERATUN MENAL LAAHE WA RAHMAH KHAYRUL MIMMAA YAJMAU’OONA.\nAnd if ye be slain in the way of God or die, then pardon from God and mercy is better than all that they amass.\nوَلَئِنْ مُّتُّمْ اَوْ قُتِلْتُمْ لَا اِلَى اللّٰهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(158)\nWA LAIN MMUTTUM AW QUTELTUM LAA ELAL LAAHE TOHSHAROON.\nFor if ye die or be slain, Verily unto God (only) shall ye be gathered.\nفَبِمَا رَحْمَةٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ لِنْتَ لَهُمْۚ وَلَوْ كُنْتَ فَظًّا غَلِيْظَ الْقَلْبِ لَانْفَضُّوْا مِنْ حَوْلِكَ فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ وَشَاوِرْهُمْ فِى الْاَمْرِۚ فَاِذَا عَزَمْتَ فَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِيْنَ‏(159)\nFA BEMAA RAHMATIN MENAL LAAHE LENTA LAHUM WA LAW KUNTA FAZZAN GHALEEZA AL-QALBE LAANFAZZOOA MIN HAWLEKA FAAA’FU A’NHUM WAASTAGHFER LAHUM WASHAAWERHUM FIL AL-AAMRE FA-EZAA A’AZAMTA FATAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAH INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL AL-MUTAWAKKELEENA.\nThus it is a mercy of God that thou art lenient unto them: Hadst thou been severe and hard-hearted, they would surely have dispersed away from around thee; Therefore forgive them and seek pardon for them; and take their counsel in the affair; But when thou art resolved, then put thou thy trust in God; For God loveth those who trust (in Him).\nاِنْ يَّنْصُرْكُمُ اللّٰهُ فَلَا غَالِبَ لَكُمْۚ وَاِنْ يَّخْذُلْكُمْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِىْ يَنْصُرُكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ ؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(160)\nIN YYANSURKUMU LAAHO FALAA GHAALEBA LAKUM WA YYAKHZULKUM FAMAN ZAL LAZEE YANSOROKUM MIN BA’DEHI WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\n(Remember O’ ye Believers!) If God helpeth you, none shall overcome you; but if He forsaketh you, who is he that would help you after that? On God then should the believers rely.\nوَمَا كَانَ لِنَبِىٍّ اَنْ يَّغُلَّؕ وَمَنْ يَّغْلُلْ يَاْتِ بِمَا غَلَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ۚ ثُمَّ تُوَفّٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(161)\nWA MAA KAANA LE-NABIYYIL AN YYAGHULLA WA MAN YYAGHLUL TAKOONOO BEMAA GHALLA YAWMA QEYAAMATE SUMMA TOWAFFAA KULLO NAFSIM MAA KASABAT WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nIt is not for any prophet (of God) to defraud; and he who defraudeth shall bring with him what he hath defrauded on the day of the Resurrection; Then shall every soul be paid what he hath earned and they shall not be dealt with unjustly.\nاَفَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ رِضْوَانَ اللّٰهِ كَمَنْۢ بَآءَ بِسَخَطٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاْوٰٮهُ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَ بِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(162)\nAAFAMANE TABA-A’L REZWAANA LAAHE KAMAM BAAA BESAKHATIN MENAL LAAHE WAMAAWAAHU JAHANNAM WA WA MASALUL MASEER.\nIs then he who abideth by the pleasure of God, like him who hath brought on himself the wrath from God, and whose abode shall be Hell? What an evil destination (it is).\nهُمْ دَرَجٰتٌ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(163)\nHUM DARAJAATUN I’NDAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO BASEER BEMAA YA’MALOON.\nThey are of diverse ranks with God; and verily God beholdeth what (all) they do.\nلَقَدْ مَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اِذْ بَعَثَ فِيْهِمْ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْ اَنْفُسِهِمْ يَتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ وَيُزَكِّيْهِمْ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ  ۚ وَاِنْ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(164)\nLAQAD MANNA LAAHO A’LAL MOAMENEEN IZ BA-A’SA FEEHIM RASOOLAM MIN ANFOSEHIM YATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATEHI WA YOZAKKEEHIM WA WA YO-A’LLEMOHOMUL KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA KAANOO MIN QABLO LAFEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nIndeed God hath conferred His favour upon the believers when He raised up an apostle Recite (Muhammad) among them from their own selves, to rehearse unto them His signs, and to purify them, and to teach them the Book (Qur’an) and Wisdom; though before this they were in manifest error.\nاَوَلَمَّاۤ اَصَابَتْكُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌ قَدْ اَصَبْتُمْ مِّثْلَيْهَا ۙ قُلْتُمْ اَنّٰى هٰذَاؕ قُلْ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اَنْفُسِكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(165)\nAAWALAMMAA AASAABATKUM MOSEEBATUN QAD AASABTUM MMESLAYHAA IZ QULTUM ANNAA HAAZAA QUL HOWA MIN I’NDIL ANFOSEKUM INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nWhat! When a misfortune befell you (at Uhud) while ye had already inflicted twice as much (on the disbelievers)’, ye said “Whence is this?” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “this is from your selves; Verily God hath power over all things.\nوَمَاۤ اَصَابَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعٰنِ فَبِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(166)\nWA MAA AASAABAKUM YAWMA AL-TAQAA AL-JAMA’AANE FA-BEIZNIL LAAHE WALEEA’LAMA MOAMENEEN.\nAnd what befell you on the day when the two hosts met, was by God’s permission and that He might know (test) the believers.\nوَلِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ نَافَقُوْا  ۖۚ وَقِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا قَاتِلُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَوِ ادْفَعُوْا ۚ قَالُوْا لَوْ نَعْلَمُ قِتَالًا لَّا تَّبَعْنٰكُمْؕ هُمْ لِلْكُفْرِ يَوْمَئِذٍ اَقْرَبُ مِنْهُمْ لِلْاِيْمَانِۚ يَقُوْلُوْنَ بِاَفْوَاهِهِمْ مَّا لَيْسَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَكْتُمُوْنَۚ‏(167)\nWALEEA’LAMA LAZEENA NAAFAQOO WA QEELAD LAHUM TA-A’ALAW QAATELOOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE AWE’ ADFAU’OOA QAALOO LAW NA’LAMO QETAALAN LAA TTABAA’NAAKUM HUM LIL-KUFRE YAWMA-EZIN AQRABO MINHUM LIL-AEEMAANE YAQOOLOONA BE-AFWAA-HEHIM MAA LAYSA FEE FEE WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAKTOMOONA.\nAnd that He might know the hypocrites; and was said unto them “Come! Fight in the way of God! or (at least) repel (the foe);” They said, “If we knew (there was a) fight, we would have followed you;” Nearer were they then (that day) to infidelity than to faith; They speak with their lips what was not in their hearts; And verily God knoweth best what they conceal.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْا لِاِخْوَانِهِمْ وَقَعَدُوْا لَوْ اَطَاعُوْنَا مَا قُتِلُوْا ؕ قُلْ فَادْرَءُوْا عَنْ اَنْفُسِكُمُ الْمَوْتَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(168)\nLAZEENA QAALOO LE-IKHWAANEHIM WAQAA’ADOOA LAW AATAAU’OONAA MAA QUTELOOA QUL FAADRAOOA A’N AANFUSEKUMU MAWTA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\n(These are those) who said unto their brethren while themselves sat (at home) “Had they (the Martyrs) obeyed us, they had not been slain;” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Ward off’ from yourselves death if ye be truthful.\nوَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ قُتِلُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَمْوَاتًا ؕ بَلْ اَحْيَآءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُوْنَۙ‏(169)\nWA LAA TAHSABANNA LAZEENA QUTELOOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE AMWAATAN BAL WA I’NDAL RABBEHIM YURZAQOONA.\nReckon not those who are slain in the way of God, to be dead; Nay! alive they are with their Lord being sustained.\nفَرِحِيْنَ بِمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ۙ وَيَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ بِالَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يَلْحَقُوْا بِهِمْ مِّنْ خَلْفِهِمْۙ اَ لَّا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَۘ‏(170)\nFAREHEENA BEMAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WA YASTABSHEROON BE-LAZEENA LAM YALHAQOO BEHIM MIN KHALFEHIM A’ZAABAN LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nRejoicing in what God of His Grace hath granted them, rejoicing for those who have not yet joined them from behind them, that no fear shall come on them nor shall they grieve.\nيَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ بِنِعْمَةٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَفَضْلٍۙ وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ  ۛۚ‏(171)\nYASTABSHEROON BENEA’MATIN MENAL LAAHE WA FAZLIN WA ANNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOAMENEEN.\nThey rejoice in the Grace from God and (His) bounty and in fact, God suffereth not to be lost the reward of the Believers.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَجَابُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَالرَّسُوْلِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَاۤ اَصَابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ  ۛؕ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا مِنْهُمْ وَاتَّقَوْا اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌۚ‏(172)\nLAZEENA ASTAJAABOOA LILLAAHE WA RASOOLE MIN BA’DE MAA AASAABAHUMU AL-QARHU LILLAZEENA AAHSANOOA MINHUM AAMANOO AJRUN A’ZEEM.\n(As far) those who did respond to the call of God and the Apostle (Muhammad) (even) after wounds inflicted on them; such of those who do good (to others) and guard (them-selves) against evil, shall have a great reward.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ قَالَ لَهُمُ النَّاسُ اِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ جَمَعُوْا لَكُمْ فَاخْشَوْهُمْ فَزَادَهُمْ اِيْمَانًا  ۖ وَّقَالُوْا حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيْلُ‏(173)\nLAZEENA QAALA LAHOMUL NAASO INNAL NAASA QAD JAMAU’OOA LAKUM FAAKHSHAWHUM FA ZAADAHUM EEMAANAW WA QAALOO HASBUNAA LAAHO WA NE’MA AL-WAKEELU.\nThose unto whom said the people, “Verily have the people mustered (strong) against you, therefore fear them!” It only increased their faith; and said they, “God is (quite) sufficient for us and the most excellent Protector is (He).\nفَانْقَلَبُوْا بِنِعْمَةٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَفَضْلٍ لَّمْ يَمْسَسْهُمْ سُوْٓءٌ ۙ وَّاتَّبَعُوْا رِضْوَانَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ ذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(174)\nFA QALABOO BENEA’MATIN MENAL LAAHE WA FAZLIN LAM YAMSASHUM SOOUN WWAATTABAU’OOA REZWAANA LAAHE WAL LAAHO ZOO FAZLIN A’ZEEM.\nThey returned, therefore, with the favour from God and (His) Grace. Without any evil even touching them and they followed the pleasure of God; and God is the Lord of Mighty Grace.\nاِنَّمَا ذٰلِكُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ يُخَوِّفُ اَوْلِيَآءَهٗ فَلَا تَخَافُوْهُمْ وَخَافُوْنِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(175)\nINNAMAA ZAALEKUMU SHAYTAANO YUKHAWFU AAWLEEAAAAH FALAA TAKHAAFOOHUM WAKHAAFOONE IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nIt is only that Satan frighteneth his friends (against supporting the Prophet), Fear them not! but fear ye Me! If ye be (true) believers.\nوَلَا يَحْزُنْكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِى الْكُفْرِۚ اِنَّهُمْ لَنْ يَّضُرُّوا اللّٰهَ شَيْئًا ؕ يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَلَّا يَجْعَلَ لَهُمْ حَظًّا فِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(176)\nWA LAA YAHZUNKA LAZEENA YUSAAREU’OONA FIL AL-KUFRE INNAHUM LAN YYAZURROOA LAAHA SHAY-ANW YOREEDO LAAHO ALLAA YAJA’ALA LAHUM HAZZAN FEE AAKHERATE WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nLet not those grieve thee, who vie in haste in infidelity, verily, never shall they harm God one whit; God intendeth that He assigneth not for them any share in the life hereafter; For them is a great chastisement.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اشْتَرَوُا الْكُفْرَ بِالْاِيْمَانِ لَنْ يَّضُرُّوا اللّٰهَ شَيْئًا ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(177)\nINNAL LAZEENA TARAWUZ KUFRA BIL-EEMAANE LAN YYAZURROOA LAAHA SHAY-ANW WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nVerily those who purchase infidelity at the cost of faith, never shall they harm God one whit! For them is a painful chastisement.\nوَلَا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّمَا نُمْلِىْ لَهُمْ خَيْرٌ لِّاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ اِنَّمَا نُمْلِىْ لَهُمْ لِيَزْدَادُوْۤا اِثْمًا ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(178)\nWA LAA YAHSABANNA LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAMAA NUMLEAA LAHUM KHAYRUL LEAANFUSEHEM INNAMAA NUMLEAA LAHUM LEYAZDAADU ISMAN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nLet not those who disbelieve think that our giving them respite is good for their selves; We only give respite to them that they may increase in sins, and for them is a disgraceful chastisement.\nمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيَذَرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلٰى مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ حَتّٰى يَمِيْزَ الْخَبِيْثَ مِنَ الطَّيِّبِؕ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُطْلِعَكُمْ عَلَى الْغَيْبِ وَ لٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَجْتَبِىْ مِنْ رُّسُلِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ فَاٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖۚ وَاِنْ تُؤْمِنُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا فَلَكُمْ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(179)\nMAA KAANA LAAHO LEEZARA MOAMENEEN A’LAA MAA ANTUM A’LAYHE HATTAA YAMEEZA KHABEESA MENAL AT-TAYBE WA MAA KAANA LAAHO LEETLEA’AKUM A’LAL GHAYBE WA LAAKENNA LAAHA YAJTABEAA MIN ROSOLEH MAN YASHAAA-O FA AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA LAM TOAMENOO WA TATTAQOO FA-LAKUM AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nIt is not for God to leave the believers in the state in which ye are, until He hath distinguished the wicked from the good and it is not for God to acquaint you with the unseen; But God chooseth from the Apostles whomsoever He pleaseth. So ye believe then in God and His apostles: and if ye believe and Guard yourselves (against evil) then for you is a great reward.\nوَلَا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَبْخَلُوْنَ بِمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ هُوَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْؕ بَلْ هُوَ شَرٌّ لَّهُمْؕ سَيُطَوَّقُوْنَ مَا بَخِلُوْا بِهٖ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ وَ لِلّٰهِ مِيْرَاثُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(180)\nWA LAA YAHSABANNA LAZEENA YABKHALOONA BEMAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI HOWA KHAYRAN LAHUM BAL HOWA HOWA LAHUM SAYUTAWQOONA MAA BAKHELOOA BEHI YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA LILLAAHE MEERAASU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nAnd let not those who are niggardly in giving what God hath granted them of His Grace, reckon it is good for them; Nay! it is bad for them; That which they have been niggardly of, shall shortly be clung to their necks on the Day of Resurrection; And God’s (alone) is the heritage of the heavens and the earth, And Verily God, of what ye do, is fully aware.\nلَقَدْ سَمِعَ اللّٰهُ قَوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ فَقِيْرٌ وَّنَحْنُ اَغْنِيَآءُ ۘ سَنَكْتُبُ مَا قَالُوْا وَقَتْلَهُمُ الْاَنْۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ ۙۚ وَّنَقُوْلُ ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(181)\nLAQAD SAMEA’A LAAHO QAWLA LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA FAQEER WA NAHNO AAGHNEEAAAU SANAKTUBU MAA QAALOO WAQATLAHUMU AL-AANBEEAAAA BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN WWANAQOOLU ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-HAREEQE.\nSurely hath God heard the saying of those who say “Aye, God is poor, and we are rich ” Certainly, shall we record what they say and their slaying the Prophets unjustly and We shall say “Taste ye the torment of burning.\nذٰ لِكَ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِۚ‏(182)\nZAA LEKA BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEKUM WA ANNAL LAAHA LAYSA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\nThis, is for what your (own) hands have forwarded before you and because God is not (in the least) unjust to (the) servants.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَهِدَ اِلَيْنَاۤ اَلَّا نُؤْمِنَ لِرَسُوْلٍ حَتّٰى يَاْتِيَنَا بِقُرْبَانٍ تَاْكُلُهُ النَّارُؕ قُلْ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِىْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَبِالَّذِىْ قُلْتُمْ فَلِمَ قَتَلْتُمُوْهُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(183)\nLAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA A’AHEDA ELAYNAA ALLAA NUMENA LE-RASOOLIN HATTAA YAATEENAA BEQURBAANIN TAAKULUHU AN-NAARU QUL QAD JAAA-AKUM RUSULUN MIN QABLEAA BIL-BAYYENAATE WA BIL-LAZEE IZ QULTUM FALEMA QATALTUMOOHUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\n(To those) who say, “Verily God hath covenanted with us that we believe not in any apostle until he presenteth to us an offering which is devoured by fire (from heaven)’, Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Indeed did come unto you apostles before me with miracles and with that which ye (now) said; Why then did ye slay them? if ye be truthful.\nفَاِنْ كَذَّبُوْكَ فَقَدْ كُذِّبَ رُسُلٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ جَآءُوْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالزُّبُرِ وَالْكِتٰبِ الْمُنِيْرِ‏(184)\nFA-IN KAZZABOOKA FAQAD KUZZEBA RUSULUN MIN QABLEKA JAAA-OO BIL-BAYYENAATE WAALZZUBURE WAL KETAABE AL-MUNEERE.\nAnd if they belie thee; then verily have already been belied apostles before thee (who) came with clear evidences (miracles) and the scriptures and the illuminating Book.\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَآئِقَةُ الْمَوْتِؕ وَاِنَّمَا تُوَفَّوْنَ اُجُوْرَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ فَمَنْ زُحْزِحَ عَنِ النَّارِ وَاُدْخِلَ الْجَنَّةَ فَقَدْ فَازَ ؕ وَمَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَاۤ اِلَّا مَتَاعُ الْغُرُوْرِ‏(185)\nKULLO NAFSIM ZAAA-EQATUL MAWT INNAMAA TOOFFAWNA AUJOORAKUM YAWMA AL-QEEMATE FAMAN ZUHZEHA A’NIL NAAR WAADKHELA JANNATA FAQAD FAAZA WA MAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA ILLAA MATAAU’U AL-GHUROORE.\nEvery self-tastes death; and verily ye shall be paid in full your recompenses on the Day of Resurrection; and whoso is removed away from the (Hell) fire and admitted into Paradise, has indeed gained his object; and the life of this world is not, but a provision of vanity.\nلَتُبْلَوُنَّ فِىْۤ اَمْوَالِكُمْ وَاَنْفُسِكُمْ وَلَتَسْمَعُنَّ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْۤا اَذًى كَثِيْرًاؕ وَاِنْ تَصْبِرُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا فَاِنَّ ذٰلِكَ مِنْ عَزْمِ الْاُمُوْرِ‏(186)\nLATUBLAWUNNA FEE ANWAALEKUM WA ANFOSEKUM WALATASMAU’UNNA MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM WA MENAN LAZEENA ASHRAKOO AZAM KASEERAN WA TASBEROOA WA TATTAQOO FA-INNAL ZAALEKA MIN A’AZME AL-AUMOORE.\nCertainly ye shall be tried in your possessions and in your (own) selves; and certainly ye shall hear from those who have been given the Book before you and those who join other gods with God, much annoyance; and if ye be patient and guard yourselves (against evil) then verily that is a matter of (very great) resolve.\nوَاِذْ اَخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِيْثَاقَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا الْكِتٰبَ لَتُبَيِّنُنَّهٗ لِلنَّاسِ وَلَا تَكْتُمُوْنَهٗ فَنَبَذُوْهُ وَرَآءَ ظُهُوْرِهِمْ وَ اشْتَرَوْا بِهٖ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًاؕ فَبِئْسَ مَا يَشْتَرُوْنَ‏(187)\nWA IZ AAKHAZA LAAHO MEESAAQA LAZEENA OOTOO KETAABA LATUBAYNUNNAH LIN-NAASE WA LAA TAKTUMOONAH FANABAZOOHU WARAAA-A ZOHOOREHIM WA TARAW BEHI SAMANAN QALEELAN FA MASALUL MAA YASHTAROONA.\nAnd (Recall thou O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when God took a pledge from those who were given the Book; “Ye shall surely make it known to mankind and ye shall not hide it; then they cast it behind their backs and bought therewith a small price; How bad (then is what they purchase ).\nلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْرَحُوْنَ بِمَاۤ اَتَوْا وَّيُحِبُّوْنَ اَنْ يُّحْمَدُوْا بِمَا لَمْ يَفْعَلُوْا فَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّهُمْ بِمَفَازَةٍ مِّنَ الْعَذَابِۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(188)\nLAA TAHSABANNA LAZEENA YAFRAHOONA BEMAA ATAW WWAYUHEBBOONA AN YYUHMADOOA BEMAA LAM YAFA’ALOOA FALAA TAHSABANNAHUM BEMAFAAZATIN MENAL A’ZAABE WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nThink not that those who rejoice for what they have brought on and love that they be praised for what they have not done, and think not that they would escape the chastisement; for them is a grievous torment.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(189)\nLILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd God’s (alone) is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and God hath power over all things.\nاِنَّ فِىْ خَلْقِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَاخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ ۚۖ‏(190)\nINNAL FEE KHALQIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WAKHTELAAFIL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE LA-AAYAATIL LEAOOLEAA ULIL ALBAABE.\nVerily, in the creation of the heavens and the earth a nd the alternation of the night and the day, there are signs for men who possess wisdom.\nالَّذِيْنَ يَذْكُرُوْنَ اللّٰهَ قِيَامًا وَّقُعُوْدًا وَّعَلٰى جُنُوْبِهِمْ وَيَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ فِىْ خَلْقِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِۚ رَبَّنَا مَا خَلَقْتَ هٰذَا بَاطِلًا ۚ سُبْحٰنَكَ فَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ‏(191)\nLAZEENA YAZKUROONA LAAHA QEEAMAN WWAQUU’OODAN WWAA’ALAA JUNOOBEHEM WA YATAFAKKAROON FEE KHALQIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE RABBANAA MAA KHALAQTA HAAZAA BAATELAN SUBHAANAKA FA QENAA A’ZAABAL NAAR.\nThose who remember God standing, and sitting and reclining on their sides and think (seriously) in the creation of the heaven and the earth, saying “O’ Our Lord! Thou hast not created (all) this in vain! Glory be to Thee! Save us then from the torment of the (Hell) fire.\nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ مَنْ تُدْخِلِ النَّارَ فَقَدْ اَخْزَيْتَهٗ ؕ وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ اَنْصَارٍ‏(192)\nRABBANAA INNAKA MAN TUDKHELE NAARAL FAQAD AAKHZAYTAH WA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN ANSAAR.\nO’ Our Lord! Whomsoever Thou causeth to enter the (Hell) fire, surely, Thou hast put him to disgrace; there is not, for the unjust, any of the helpers.\nرَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّنَا سَمِعْنَا مُنَادِيًا يُّنَادِىْ لِلْاِيْمَانِ اَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِرَبِّكُمْ فَاٰمَنَّا  ۖ رَبَّنَا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَا وَكَفِّرْ عَنَّا سَيِّاٰتِنَا وَتَوَفَّنَا مَعَ الْاَبْرَارِۚ‏(193)\nRABBANAA INNANAA SAMEA’NAA MUNAADEEA YYUNAADEAA LIL-AEEMAANE AN AAMENOO BE-RABBEKUM FA AAMANNAA RABBANAA FAGH-FIR LANAA ZUNOOBANAA WAKAFFER WAGH SAYAAATENAA WATAWAFFANAA LAAHA ABRAARE.\nO’ Our Lord! We have indeed heard the voice of a Crier (Apostle), calling (us) unto faith, saying “Believe ye in your Lord!” and we did believe. O’ Our Lord! therefore “Forgive us then our sins and remove away from us our evil deeds, and cause us to die with the virtuous ones.\nرَبَّنَا وَاٰتِنَا مَا وَعَدتَّنَا عَلٰى رُسُلِكَ وَلَا تُخْزِنَا يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ اِنَّكَ لَا تُخْلِفُ الْمِيْعَادَ‏(194)\nRABBANAA WA FID MAA WAA’ADTTANAA A’LAA RUSULEKA WA LAA TUKHZENAA YAWMA QEYAAMATE INNAKA LAA TUKHLEFU AL-MEEA’AADA.\nO’ Our Lord! and give us what Thou didst promise us through thy apostles, and disgrace us not on the Day of Resurrection; Verily, Thou breakest not Thy promise.\nفَاسْتَجَابَ لَهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ اَنِّىْ لَاۤ اُضِيْعُ عَمَلَ عَامِلٍ مِّنْكُمْ مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰىۚ بَعْضُكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْضٍۚ فَالَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا وَاُخْرِجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ وَاُوْذُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِىْ وَقٰتَلُوْا وَقُتِلُوْا لَاُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَلَاُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُۚ ثَوَابًا مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ عِنْدَهٗ حُسْنُ الثَّوَابِ‏(195)\nFAASTAJAABA LAHUM RABBOHUM AANNEAA LAA AUZEEU’U A’AMALA A’AAMELIN MINKUM MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA BA’ZOKUM MIN ELAA FAL LAZEENA HAAJAROO WA UKHREJOO MIN DEYAAREHIM WAAWZOOA FEE SABEELEAA WA QAATALOO WAQUTELOOA LAAKAFFERANNA A’NHUM SAYYEAATEHIM WALAADKHELANNAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO SAWAABAN MIN I’NDIL LAAHE WA LAAHO I’NDAHU HUSNU AS-SAWAABE.\nSo their Lord did respond to them (saying) “I will not suffer the work of any of you that worketh to be lost, be he male or female, the one of you being from the other, They, therefore, who did migrate and were turned out of their homes and suffered in My way and who fought and were slain, I will most certainly blot out their sins from them, and I will most certainly admit them into gardens beneath which flow streams; A reward from God! and God! Verily with Him (only) is the Excellent Reward.\nلَا يَغُرَّنَّكَ تَقَلُّبُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِى الْبِلَادِؕ‏(196)\nLAA YAGHURRANNAKA TAQALLUBU LAZEENA KAFAROO FIL AL-BELAADE.\nLet not deceive thee the (prosperous) going about of those who disbelieve in the cities.\nمَتَاعٌ قَلِيْلٌ ثُمَّ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَ بِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ‏(197)\nLIL-MOTAALLAQAATE QALEELUN SUMMA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA MASALUL MEHAAD.\nA brief enjoyment (it is)! Thereafter their abode is Hell and how bad the resting place (it is)!\nلٰكِنِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا نُزُلًا مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ لِّلْاَبْرَارِ‏(198)\nLAAKENE LAZEENA TAQAW RABBAHUM LAHUM LAHUM TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA NOZOLAM MIN I’NDIL LAAH WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE KHAYRUL LLELAABRAARE.\nBut as to those who fear (the wrath of) their Lord, for them are the gardens beneath which flow the rivers, therein shall they abide for ever. Such is their reception with God; and whatever is with God is the best for the righteous ones.\nوَاِنَّ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ لَمَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِمْ خٰشِعِيْنَ لِلّٰهِ ۙ لَا يَشْتَرُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ اَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(199)\nWA INNA MIN AHLIL KETAABE LAMAN YOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WA MAA UNZELA ELAYKUM WA MAA UNZELA ELAYHIM KHAASHEE’EENA LILLAAHE LAA YASHTAROONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE SAMANAN QALEELAA OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM AJROHUM I’NDAL RABBEHIM INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nAnd Verily among the people of the Book are those who believe in God, and in what hath been sent down unto you and in what hath been sent down unto them, humbling themselves before God, They sell not the signs of God for a mean price; These! for them is their recompense with their Lord; aye! God is quick in reckoning.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اصْبِرُوْا وَصَابِرُوْا وَرَابِطُوْا وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(200)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT ASBEROOA WASAABEROOA WARAABETOOA WAT TAQUL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO’ ye who believe! be patient and vie with, in endurance and be ever-garrisoned; and fear (the wrath of) God, that ye may be successful.",
  "merits": "In this Surah, there are a total of 200 verses and it was revealed in Madinah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites Surah Ali-’Imran on Friday, then until the setting of the sun, he will be showered by the Mercy of Allah (s.w.t.) and the angels will beg for his forgiveness.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has also recommended this Surah for those women who are not able to conceive. The Surah should be written using saffron and then given to her to wear as a talisman and by the Will of Allah (s.w.t.) she will conceive.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a person faces hardship in earning his livelihood, he should write this Surah and wear it as a talisman and Allah (s.w.t.) will increase his sustenance greatly. The Imam (a.s.) also said that if anyone recites both [Surah al-Baqarah](A6) and Aal-e-Imraan, then these Surahs will come in the shape of clouds on the day of judgement to protect him from the scorching heat."
}
